,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468762553,"data":"       | analysisWe have K = (0.789..., -5.71...), K' = (-1.602..., 11.5889...). B = (0,0). So points B, K, K' are not collinear. So O_c should exist.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468763983,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468765194,"data":"       | Our circumcenter_from_origin function solves linear system using coordinates of K and K' (not B). But we need to solve for center (h,k) satisfying h*x1 + k*y1 = (x1^2 + y1^2)/2 and similarly for x2,y2. That should give O_c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468766744,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468767866,"data":"       | Let's compute O_c for n=5 using that function.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468769075,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468770246,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef circumcenter_origin(p1, p2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468771515,"data":"       |     x1, y1 = p1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468772688,"data":"       |     x2, y2 = p2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468773864,"data":"       |     A = np.array([[x1, y1], [x2, y2]], dtype=float)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468776051,"data":"       |     b = np.array([(x1**2 + y1**2)/2.0, (x2**2 + y2**2)/2.0], dtype=float)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.46877741,"data":"       |     det = np.linalg.det(A)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468778635,"data":"       |     if abs(det) \u003c 1e-12:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468780228,"data":"       |         return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468781424,"data":"       |     sol = np.linalg.solve(A, b)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.468782624,"data":"       |     return (sol[0], sol[1])\n"}
