,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.469066782,"data":"     [Reasoning] (482 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.46906825,"data":"       | analysisSympy gave expression 1/2 - 3/2 + sqrt(5) = sqrt(5) - 1. That's interesting: c_ratio = sqrt(5) - 1 ≈ 2.236 - 1 = 1.236. Wait AB length cannot exceed BC (which is 1). But we used BC=1 scaling; c_ratio \u003e 1 indicates AB \u003e BC, which may be possible. Indeed AB can be longer than BC.\n"}
