,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.470088021,"data":"       | analysisWhoa ratio ~21.76, far from earlier values (~8). Something is off. Perhaps our formula for t is wrong because we derived assuming O_T is intersection of perpendicular bisector of BK and perpendicular to BN, but we might have misapplied due to K being below BC (negative y). The circle tangent to BN at B passes through K which is below BC. The intersection with BC yields a point T on BC near B (since K is below). t should be small (makes sense). Indeed we got t ≈ 0.0345, which is plausible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.470090145,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.470091357,"data":"       | But earlier for finite n (n=6) we got BT about maybe 0. something? Let's compute for n=6 using earlier method to see BT.\n"}
