,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.470296885,"data":"       | analysisWe see t (BT) is increasing with n: for n=5, t≈4.21, for n=6, t≈6.71, n=7 t≈10.92, n=8 t≈17.63, etc. So t grows roughly like something exponential (maybe φ^{n}). Indeed t appears to be about F_{n+2}? Let's check: For n=5, F_{7}=13, t=4.21 not close. But maybe t corresponds to something like (F_{n+2} - something). Let's compute t / L maybe.\n"}
