,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471434448,"data":"       | Compute intersection of circles (A and K). Solve for intersection points of two circles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471435752,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471436956,"data":"       | We can compute intersection using standard formula: given two circles with centers O1,O2 and radii R1,R2, the intersection points can be found. Since we know one intersection is A (computed), we can compute the other K by reflecting A across line connecting centers? Not exactly. But we can compute both intersection points and pick the one not equal to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47143876,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47143994,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can compute K as the second intersection of circles using geometry: The line connecting the two centers O1O2, the intersection points lie symmetric about that line. We can compute using vector formulas.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471441475,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471442628,"data":"       | Simplify: Use sympy's Circle.intersection with numeric substitution may be faster.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47144392,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471445036,"data":"       | But we need to compute condition function f(r) = distance(N, O_BKK') - radius_BKK'. Let's compute numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471446361,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471447528,"data":"       | Let's implement numeric function compute_ratio_numeric(c0,d0,r) returning ratio and condition value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471448845,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471450011,"data":"       | We'll need to compute K and K' etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471451192,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471452329,"data":"       | Let's code using numpy for speed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471453517,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471454635,"data":"       | But we need to compute intersection of circles (A,E,F) and (A,B,C). Use analytic formulas.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471455956,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471457098,"data":"       | Let's write functions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471458239,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471459378,"data":"       | First, compute F and E coordinates as earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471460582,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471461888,"data":"       | Then compute line BF and CE intersection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471463109,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471464238,"data":"       | Line BF: passes through (0,0) and F; param t*F.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471465462,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471466615,"data":"       | Line CE: passes through C and E; param C + s*(E - C). Solve for intersection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471469145,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47147033,"data":"       | Solve linear equations: t*F = C + s*(E - C). Two unknowns t,s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471471569,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471472715,"data":"       | We can solve using 2x2 linear system.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471473953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471475097,"data":"       | Then compute A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471476409,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471477565,"data":"       | Now compute circumcenter of triangle ABC: Use formula for circumcenter given coordinates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471478877,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471480028,"data":"       | Circumcenter of triangle with points P1,P2,P3 can be computed using perpendicular bisectors or using linear algebra.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471481388,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471482517,"data":"       | We'll implement function circumcenter(P1,P2,P3).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471483712,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47148484,"data":"       | Similarly for triangle AEF.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471486005,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471487163,"data":"       | Now compute intersection of circles: we have centers O1,O2 and radii R1,R2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471488448,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471489555,"data":"       | We know one intersection is A. Compute the other K.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471490786,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471491967,"data":"       | Method: Let d = distance between centers O1O2. Let ex = (O2 - O1)/d (unit vector). Let a = (R1^2 - R2^2 + d^2) / (2d). Let h = sqrt(R1^2 - a^2). Then point P = O1 + a * ex is the point along line connecting centers where line of intersection points crosses. Then intersection points are P ± h * ey, where ey is a unit vector perpendicular to ex (rotate by 90°). Choose the one not equal to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47149386,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471494956,"data":"       | Thus we can compute K.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471496123,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471497267,"data":"       | Now compute line EF; reflect K across line EF to get K'.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471498505,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471499652,"data":"       | Reflection of point across line defined by two points can be done using vector projection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471500953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471502136,"data":"       | Given line defined by points E and F, compute unit direction vector u = (F - E) / |F - E|. Then projection of point K onto line: proj = E + u * ((K - E)·u). Then reflected point K' = 2*proj - K.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471503639,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471504755,"data":"       | Now compute N: foot of perpendicular from D to line EF: same as projection of D onto EF.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471506062,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471507551,"data":"       | Now compute condition: compute circumcenter of triangle B K K' (call O_BKK) and radius R_BKK = distance(O_BKK, B). Then compute distance from O_BKK to N; condition is that distance equals radius. So f(r) = distance(O_BKK,N) - R_BKK.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47151038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471511561,"data":"       | Now compute T: circle through B and K tangent to BN at B. Center O_T is intersection of line perpendicular to BN at B (call L1) and perpendicular bisector of BK (call L2). Compute O_T as intersection of two lines.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471513095,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471514285,"data":"       | Line L1: passes through B and direction perpendicular to BN. BN vector = N - B. So direction of L1 is perpendicular to BN: rotate BN by 90°.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471515726,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471516853,"data":"       | Line L2: perpendicular bisector of BK: passes through midpoint M of B and K, direction perpendicular to BK vector.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471518187,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471519335,"data":"       | Intersect lines to get O_T.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471520543,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471521709,"data":"       | Now find intersection of circle centered at O_T radius R_T = distance(O_T,B) with line BC (x-axis). Solve for x coordinate.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471523079,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471524276,"data":"       | Since B at (0,0) is on circle, we know one intersection is x=0. The other solution x_T can be found by solving equation (x - O_T.x)^2 + (0 - O_T.y)^2 = R_T^2. Expand: (x - O_T.x)^2 = R_T^2 - O_T.y^2. Since R_T^2 = O_T.x^2 + O_T.y^2 (distance from O_T to B). So RHS = O_T.x^2 + O_T.y^2 - O_T.y^2 = O_T.x^2. So equation reduces to (x - O_T.x)^2 = O_T.x^2 =\u003e sqrt both sides: |x - O_T.x| = |O_T.x|. Solutions: x - O_T.x = ± O_T.x =\u003e x = 0 (when minus sign) or x = 2 O_T.x (when plus sign). Indeed, the circle intersecting x-axis yields points at x = 0 (B) and x = 2 O_T.x (the other). So T_x = 2*O_T.x.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471526608,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471527745,"data":"       | Thus T = (2*O_T.x, 0). Good! So we don't need solving.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471528975,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471530196,"data":"       | Thus CT = |C.x - 2*O_T.x|, BT = |2*O_T.x| = 2*|O_T.x| (since O_T.x positive? Might be positive). Since B at 0, O_T.x likely positive (since circle passes through B and K which is to right of B). So T_x = 2*O_T.x \u003e 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471531743,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471532888,"data":"       | Thus ratio = (|a - 2*O_T.x| * NB) / (2*O_T.x * NE).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471534109,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471535243,"data":"       | Now we can compute ratio numeric.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471536449,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471537569,"data":"       | Now we need to solve f(r) = 0 for r \u003e 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471538816,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471539965,"data":"       | Let's implement numeric root-finding for given c0,d0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471541211,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471542325,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport math\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471543582,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47154492,"data":"       | def circumcenter(P1, P2, P3):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471546176,"data":"       |     # compute circumcenter of triangle given points (x,y)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471548452,"data":"       |     x1,y1 = P1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471549639,"data":"       |     x2,y2 = P2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471550848,"data":"       |     x3,y3 = P3\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471552085,"data":"       |     # using perpendicular bisector intersection formula\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471553347,"data":"       |     d = 2*(x1*(y2-y3) + x2*(y3-y1) + x3*(y1-y2))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471554565,"data":"       |     if abs(d) \u003c 1e-12:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471555758,"data":"       |         return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47155695,"data":"       |     ux = ((x1**2 + y1**2)*(y2 - y3) + (x2**2 + y2**2)*(y3 - y1) + (x3**2 + y3**2)*(y1 - y2)) / d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47155836,"data":"       |     uy = ((x1**2 + y1**2)*(x3 - x2) + (x2**2 + y2**2)*(x1 - x3) + (x3**2 + y3**2)*(x2 - x1)) / d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471559668,"data":"       |     return (ux, uy)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471560878,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471562012,"data":"       | def intersect_circles(O1, R1, O2, R2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471563249,"data":"       |     # returns two intersection points (list of tuples). assumes circles intersect.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47156453,"data":"       |     x1,y1 = O1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471565728,"data":"       |     x2,y2 = O2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471566876,"data":"       |     dx = x2 - x1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471568029,"data":"       |     dy = y2 - y1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471569229,"data":"       |     d = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471570446,"data":"       |     if d == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471571617,"data":"       |         return []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471572797,"data":"       |     # a = (R1^2 - R2^2 + d^2) / (2d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471574018,"data":"       |     a = (R1**2 - R2**2 + d**2) / (2*d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471575218,"data":"       |     # h^2 = R1^2 - a^2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471576391,"data":"       |     h_sq = R1**2 - a**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471577551,"data":"       |     if h_sq \u003c -1e-12:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471578773,"data":"       |         return []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471579988,"data":"       |     h = math.sqrt(max(0.0, h_sq))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471581193,"data":"       |     # point P2 = O1 + a*(O2-O1)/d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471582387,"data":"       |     xm = x1 + a * dx / d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471583582,"data":"       |     ym = y1 + a * dy / d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471584759,"data":"       |     # intersection points:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471585938,"data":"       |     rx = -dy * (h / d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471587085,"data":"       |     ry = dx * (h / d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471588269,"data":"       |     p1 = (xm + rx, ym + ry)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471589511,"data":"       |     p2 = (xm - rx, ym - ry)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471590682,"data":"       |     return [p1, p2]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471591882,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471594207,"data":"       | def reflect_point_across_line(P, A, B):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47159548,"data":"       |     # reflect point P across line AB\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471596701,"data":"       |     # line defined by points A,B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471597952,"data":"       |     # compute projection onto line\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471599171,"data":"       |     ax, ay = A\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471600383,"data":"       |     bx, by = B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471601529,"data":"       |     px, py = P\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471602719,"data":"       |     # direction vector of line\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471603916,"data":"       |     dx = bx - ax\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47160506,"data":"       |     dy = by - ay\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471606258,"data":"       |     # compute projection scalar t = ((P-A)·(dx,dy)) / (dx^2+dy^2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471607587,"data":"       |     t = ((px-ax)*dx + (py-ay)*dy) / (dx*dx + dy*dy)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471608823,"data":"       |     projx = ax + t*dx\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471610475,"data":"       |     projy = ay + t*dy\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471611683,"data":"       |     # reflected point\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471612827,"data":"       |     rx = 2*projx - px\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471613977,"data":"       |     ry = 2*projy - py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471615129,"data":"       |     return (rx, ry)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.47161631,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471617435,"data":"       | def foot_of_perpendicular(P, A, B):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471618695,"data":"       |     # foot from point P to line AB (same as projection)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.471620005,"data":"       |     return reflect_point_across_line(P, A, B)  # Actually reflection across line gives mirror; foot is projection (midpoint between P and its reflection)\n"}
