,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.475184281,"data":"       | analysisSeems ratio converges to around 2.06974... for even n (n=4 gave 2.07846, n=6 gave 2.07097, n=8 gave 2.06992, n=10 gave 2.06976, n=12 gave 2.06974). So limit appears around 2.06974... maybe 2.06974... Let's compute for larger n (e.g., n=14,16). We'll need to compute Fibonacci numbers for large n; but we can compute using Python's integer big.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.475186074,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.475187209,"data":"       | Compute for n=14 (c0=377,d0=610). Let's do.\n"}
