,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.477717014,"data":"       | Nevertheless, there might be known relationships: The reflection of K across EF, K', lies on the circumcircle of ABC? Actually if quadrilateral KNK'B is cyclic, then K' lies on the circumcircle of BKN? Wait condition: KNK'B is cyclic. So points K,N,K',B lie on a circle. Since K and B are already on circumcircle Ω, but N is not on Ω generally, K' is not on Ω generally. So cyclic condition imposes some relationship.\n"}
