,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481539785,"data":"       | We can use sum-to-product identities: sin B + sin C = 2 sin((B+C)/2) cos((B-C)/2). Cos B - cos C = -2 sin((B+C)/2) sin((B-C)/2). Actually cos B - cos C = -2 sin((B+C)/2) sin((B-C)/2). So:\n"}
