,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48156079,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481561953,"data":"       | Thus A = - sec((B+C)/2) * (cos((B-C)/2), sin((B-C)/2)).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481563235,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481564489,"data":"       | Thus A is a point on the line through origin with direction angle (B-C)/2, at distance sec((B+C)/2) from origin (since magnitude of vector (cos((B-C)/2), sin((B-C)/2)) is 1). So |A| = sec((B+C)/2). Since sec = 1 / cos. So distance from O to A is 1 / cos((B+C)/2). Since B+C = π - A (since A + B + C = π). So (B+C)/2 = (π - A)/2 = π/2 - A/2. So cos((B+C)/2) = cos(π/2 - A/2) = sin(A/2). So sec((B+C)/2) = 1 / sin(A/2). So |A| = 1 / sin(A/2). So A lies on ray from O opposite direction angle (B-C)/2, at distance 1 / sin(A/2). Since O is incircle center.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481566779,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481567913,"data":"       | Thus coordinates of A are:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.481569109,"data":"       | \n"}
