,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.486967239,"data":"       | Nevertheless, maybe K is the exsimilicenter of incircle and circumcircle. Let's test numerically for a random triangle: compute exsimilicenter as intersection of line OI with line connecting points where incircle and circumcircle are externally tangent? Actually external homothety center is the point X such that lines from X to the two circles are tangent to both circles. It lies on line OI, and satisfies OX / IX = R / r (R circumradius, r incircle radius). It also lies on line through A and the point where the A-mixtilinear incircle touches circumcircle? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.486969439,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.486970627,"data":"       | But K might be that exsimilicenter. If so, K lies on line OI. Then K' is reflection across EF, maybe some symmetry.\n"}
