,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488026027,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48802717,"data":"       | Thus s - b = p, s - c = q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488028373,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48802951,"data":"       | Now s = (a + b + c)/2 = (F_{n+2} + b + c)/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488030736,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488031878,"data":"       | We can compute b and c: b = s - p, c = s - q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488033736,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488035587,"data":"       | Now we can also compute AF = s - a = s - F_{n+2}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488037474,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488039118,"data":"       | Thus AF = s - a = s - (p+q) = s - p - q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488042223,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488043513,"data":"       | Now we also have BF = p.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488044676,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48804581,"data":"       | Thus AB = c = BF + AF = p + (s - p - q) = s - q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488047072,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488048202,"data":"       | But we already have c = s - q, consistent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488049403,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488050545,"data":"       | Similarly AC = b = s - p.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488051733,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488052894,"data":"       | Now we can compute coordinates using perhaps more convenient parameterization: Use triangle with incircle radius r and known tangency distances.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488054317,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488055472,"data":"       | There is known formula for side lengths in terms of r and angles: b = r (cot B/2 + cot C/2). But maybe we can express r in terms of p, q and angle A? Let's derive.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488056961,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48805812,"data":"       | Given incircle radius r, the distance from incircle center I to side BC is r (vertical). The distances from I to AB and AC are also r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48805953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48806068,"data":"       | The coordinates we used earlier: B = (0,0), C = (p+q,0), I = (p,r). This is consistent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488061988,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488063134,"data":"       | Now we can compute line AB: passes through B (0,0) and F (touchpoint). But we can also compute F coordinates using geometry: Since BF = p, AF = s - p - q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488064578,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488066033,"data":"       | But we have coordinates for F earlier: (p*(p^2 - r^2)/(p^2 + r^2), 2 p^2 r/(p^2 + r^2)). Let's verify that BF distance equals p.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488068694,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488069863,"data":"       | Compute distance between B (0,0) and F: sqrt(F.x^2 + F.y^2). Let's compute symbolic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488071192,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48807237,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeFx = p*(p**2 - r**2)/(p**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488073681,"data":"       | Fy = 2*p**2*r/(p**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488074898,"data":"       | BF_sq = sp.simplify(Fx**2 + Fy**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488076117,"data":"       | BF_sq\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488077283,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488078438,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488079625,"data":"       | Fx = p*(p**2 - r**2)/(p**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.48808086,"data":"       | Fy = 2*p**2*r/(p**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488082047,"data":"       | BF_sq = sp.simplify(Fx**2 + Fy**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488083283,"data":"       | BF_sq\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.488084432,"data":"       | \n"}
