,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489472507,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489473713,"data":"       | Given circle tangent to BN at B and passing through B and K. For a circle tangent to line BN at B, the radius at B is perpendicular to BN. So the center O_T of this circle lies on line through B perpendicular to BN. Also O_T is equidistant from B and K (since both points on circle). So O_T is intersection of perpendicular line to BN at B with perpendicular bisector of BK.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489475562,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489476738,"data":"       | Thus we can compute O_T as intersection of line L1: through B with direction perpendicular to BN (i.e., direction vector = rotate BN by 90°), and line L2: perpendicular bisector of BK.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489478291,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489479417,"data":"       | Then radius R_T = distance O_T to B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489480647,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489481804,"data":"       | Then find intersection of this circle with line BC (x-axis) besides B. Since BC is x-axis (y=0). So we can solve for intersection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489483219,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489484391,"data":"       | Compute T coordinate.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489485583,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489486761,"data":"       | Then compute distances: CT = distance between C (p+q,0) and T (x_T,0) = |(p+q) - x_T|. Since T lies between B and C maybe? Not sure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489488172,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489489299,"data":"       | BT = distance between B (0,0) and T = |x_T|.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489490532,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.489491687,"data":"       | NB = distance between N and B (distance from N to B). NE = distance between N and E.\n"}
