,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490708782,"data":"       | analysisThe matrix A_mat becomes singular for some root where BN is parallel to BK, causing the perpendicular bisector to be parallel to BN, leading to infinite solutions for center O_T? In that case, the circle tangent to BN at B and passing through K may be undefined (if BN is tangent to circle at B, the center must lie on line perpendicular to BN at B, but also on perpendicular bisector of BK. If these lines are parallel, there is no intersection (unless they coincide). This may happen for certain configurations where K lies on line through B perpendicular to BN? Actually if BK is perpendicular to BN, then perpendicular bisector of BK is parallel to BN (since BK perpendicular to BN, its perpendicular bisector is also perpendicular to BK, thus parallel to BN). Then there is no unique circle tangent to BN at B passing through K (since the center would be intersection of two parallel lines). In such case, the condition of circle tangent to BN at B and passing through K may be impossible. However, the problem statement says \"The circle tangent to line BN and passing through B and K intersects BC again at T ≠ B\". This implies such a circle exists, so BN must not be parallel to BK. So among roots, we need to discard those where BN is parallel to BK (i.e., cross product zero). So we need to filter roots.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490712465,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490713668,"data":"       | Thus for each root r, compute BN direction and BK direction, ensure they are not parallel (i.e., cross product not near zero). Then compute ratio.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490715129,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490716257,"data":"       | Now for n=3 earlier we got root r≈0.7851, and the ratio ~14.5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49071758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.490718755,"data":"       | Now for n=5 (p=5, q=8) we need to find roots that satisfy geometry and compute ratio.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49072187,"data":"       | \n"}
