,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491466814,"data":"       | Let's attempt to find exact expression by solving analytically for p=1, q=φ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491468147,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491469288,"data":"       | We have r root ~0.4452013909.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491470463,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491473116,"data":"       | We can attempt to solve the cyclic condition analytically for p=1, q=φ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491474453,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491475625,"data":"       | But the condition is determinant = 0, which may reduce to polynomial equation in r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491476937,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491478131,"data":"       | We can compute symbolic expression for determinant with p=1, q=φ (symbolic sqrt(5)). Then factor and solve for r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491479534,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491480669,"data":"       | Let's attempt using sympy with rational approximation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491481894,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491483342,"data":"       | But earlier we had difficulty due to heavy symbolic expression for K. However, maybe we can compute K using intersection of circles analytically using algebraic formulas that involve solving quadratic; we can derive coordinates of K directly using known formulas for intersection of two circles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491485033,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491486193,"data":"       | Given circles: Circle1: circumcircle of ABC with center O1 and radius R1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.4914875,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49148863,"data":"       | Circle2: circumcircle of AFE with center O2 and radius R2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491489878,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491491042,"data":"       | We can compute O1, O2, R1, R2 analytically in terms of p,q,r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491492331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491493565,"data":"       | Then intersection points are given by solving linear equations: the line connecting the intersection points is perpendicular to line O1O2 and passes through point P2 (the point along O1O2 at distance a from O1). The coordinates of K can be expressed using these formulas.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491495211,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491496357,"data":"       | Thus we can get K coordinates as:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491497559,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491498722,"data":"       | Let d = |O2 - O1|.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491499912,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49150109,"data":"       | Let a = (R1^2 - R2^2 + d^2) / (2 d). This is distance from O1 to the line of intersection along O1O2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491502428,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491503541,"data":"       | Let h^2 = R1^2 - a^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491504716,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491505899,"data":"       | Let unit vector u = (O2 - O1) / d.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491507109,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49150828,"data":"       | Then the midpoint of the chord is P = O1 + a * u.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491509513,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491510661,"data":"       | Then the intersection points are P ± h * (perp vector to u). Choose the one not equal to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491512012,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491513193,"data":"       | Thus K coordinates can be expressed in terms of O1, O2, R1, R2, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491516214,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491517393,"data":"       | Thus we can compute K analytically without solving quadratic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49151869,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491520404,"data":"       | Thus we can derive determinant expression more tractably.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491521664,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491522814,"data":"       | Let's attempt to compute O1 (circumcenter of ABC) analytically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491524077,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491525232,"data":"       | Given B=(0,0), C=(p+q,0), A coordinates as earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491526486,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49152768,"data":"       | But we can compute O1 using formula for circumcenter of triangle with base BC on x-axis: O1's x-coordinate is (p+q)/2 (midpoint of BC) because BC is chord of circumcircle symmetrical? Actually not necessarily; for any triangle with base BC on x-axis, the circumcenter lies on perpendicular bisector of BC, which is vertical line x = (p+q)/2. So O1 = ((p+q)/2, y0). y0 is determined by distance to B: R1^2 = ((p+q)/2)^2 + y0^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491529658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491531008,"data":"       | Similarly, O1 must be equidistant to A: (x_A - (p+q)/2)^2 + (y_A - y0)^2 = R1^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49153228,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49153342,"data":"       | Thus we can solve for y0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491534584,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491535727,"data":"       | But perhaps easier: Use sympy to compute O1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491536944,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491538102,"data":"       | But we can also compute O2: circumcenter of triangle AFE. Since F and E are points of tangency; but we can compute O2 via sympy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491539467,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491540646,"data":"       | But perhaps we can find K using known property: K is the second intersection of circles; we can compute K as described.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491541984,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491543114,"data":"       | Thus we need O1, O2, R1, R2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491544297,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491545443,"data":"       | Let's compute O1 analytically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491546619,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491547749,"data":"       | Given B=(0,0), C=(a,0) where a = p+q.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491548955,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491550125,"data":"       | Midpoint M_bc = (a/2, 0). Perpendicular bisector is vertical line x = a/2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491551417,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491552574,"data":"       | Thus O1 = (a/2, y_O1). Determine y_O1 by solving distance to B equals distance to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491553884,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491555042,"data":"       | Thus R1^2 = (a/2)^2 + y_O1^2 = (x_A - a/2)^2 + (y_A - y_O1)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491556295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491557475,"data":"       | Thus we can solve for y_O1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49156053,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491561717,"data":"       | Let's derive expression.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.4915629,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491564013,"data":"       | Let xA, yA as earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491565179,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491566322,"data":"       | Equation: (a/2)^2 + y_O1^2 = (xA - a/2)^2 + (yA - y_O1)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491567584,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491568716,"data":"       | Simplify: (a/2)^2 + y_O1^2 = (xA - a/2)^2 + yA^2 - 2 yA y_O1 + y_O1^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491569998,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49157116,"data":"       | Cancel y_O1^2 both sides.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491572331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491573469,"data":"       | Thus (a/2)^2 = (xA - a/2)^2 + yA^2 - 2 yA y_O1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491574671,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491575813,"data":"       | Thus solve for y_O1:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491576984,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491578151,"data":"       | 2 yA y_O1 = (xA - a/2)^2 + yA^2 - (a/2)^2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491579335,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491580522,"data":"       | Thus y_O1 = ((xA - a/2)^2 + yA^2 - (a/2)^2) / (2 yA).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491581757,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491582871,"data":"       | Thus O1 = (a/2, y_O1).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491584031,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491585161,"data":"       | Now O2: circumcenter of triangle AFE.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491586358,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491587525,"data":"       | We can compute O2 using standard formula for circumcenter of three points. That may be messy but we can compute using sympy and then simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491588929,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491590151,"data":"       | But perhaps we can avoid O2 by using property: Since A, F, E are points, we can compute O2 coordinates using intersection of perpendicular bisectors of AF and AE.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491591582,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491592756,"data":"       | But maybe we can compute O2 directly using sympy and then simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491594082,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491595489,"data":"       | Given the complexity, we can attempt to compute the cyclic condition determinant using these formulas and then simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491596863,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49159802,"data":"       | But perhaps there is a simpler approach: The cyclic condition B,N,K,K' cyclic may be equivalent to some angle equality that can be expressed in terms of known angles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491599482,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491600671,"data":"       | Given the incircle geometry, perhaps the condition reduces to something like ∠KBN = ∠K'BN? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491602081,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491603237,"data":"       | Let's attempt to compute the condition using angles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49160658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49160779,"data":"       | Quadrilateral B,N,K,K' cyclic means that ∠B N K = ∠B K' N (angles subtended by BK). Since K' is reflection of K across EF, we can relate angles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491609284,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491610431,"data":"       | But maybe we can use property: The reflection across EF changes orientation relative to line AI, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491611764,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491613005,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can compute using vector geometry: The condition that four points are concyclic is equivalent to (B - N)·(K - K') = (B - K)·(N - K')? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491614504,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491615638,"data":"       | But there is known condition: For points P, Q, R, S, they are concyclic iff (P - Q)·(R - S) + (P - S)·(Q - R) = (P - R)·(Q - S). Not recall.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491617095,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491618295,"data":"       | Better to use determinant condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491619538,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491620702,"data":"       | Thus we may need to compute determinant symbolic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491621944,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491623085,"data":"       | Given we can treat p=1, q=φ, we can compute the determinant expression as a rational function of r (including sqrt(5) from φ). Then solve for r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491624553,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491625712,"data":"       | Let's attempt to compute determinant for p=1, q=phi symbolically using sympy with sqrt(5) symbolic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491627025,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491628192,"data":"       | We'll define p=1, q=phi (symbolic), r as variable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491629446,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491630589,"data":"       | Compute points A,B,C,F,E,N,K,K' using sympy rational functions. Then compute determinant.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491631877,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491633068,"data":"       | But we need to compute K using intersection of circles using analytic formulas (not solving with sympy's intersection method which may be heavy). However, we can implement the intersection formula ourselves.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491634603,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491635743,"data":"       | Let's implement in sympy:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491636931,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491638253,"data":"       | - Compute O1 = (a/2, y_O1) as derived.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491639457,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491640622,"data":"       | - Compute R1^2 = (a/2)^2 + y_O1**2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491641794,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491642949,"data":"       | - Compute O2: use sympy's circumcenter function for points A,F,E. That may be okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491644233,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491645359,"data":"       | - Compute R2^2 = (O2.distance(A))**2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491646577,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491649651,"data":"       | - Compute vector d = O2 - O1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491650873,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49165201,"data":"       | - Compute d_norm = sqrt(d·d).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491653235,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491654455,"data":"       | - Compute a_dist = (R1^2 - R2^2 + d_norm**2) / (2*d_norm).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491655725,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491656871,"data":"       | - Compute h_sq = R1^2 - a_dist**2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491658064,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491659197,"data":"       | - Compute unit vector u = d / d_norm.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491660399,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491661547,"data":"       | - Compute point P = O1 + a_dist * u.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491662747,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491663909,"data":"       | - Then K = P + sqrt(h_sq) * perp(u) (choose sign that gives K not equal A). Perp(u) = (-u_y, u_x).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491665217,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491666379,"data":"       | - Compute K' as reflection across line EF: we can use formula for reflection of point across line defined by two points.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491667755,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491668906,"data":"       | Sympy can handle reflection.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491670075,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491671239,"data":"       | Thus we can compute K coordinates symbolically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491672447,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49167362,"data":"       | Potentially the expressions will involve sqrt's (including sqrt of h_sq). However, we can keep them symbolic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49167496,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491676126,"data":"       | But the cyclic condition determinant may simplify, maybe eliminating sqrt's, leading to polynomial equation in r.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491677487,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491678611,"data":"       | Let's try.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491679755,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491680905,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491682181,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491683477,"data":"       | # define symbols\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491684654,"data":"       | r = sp.symbols('r', positive=True, real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49168586,"data":"       | phi = (1+sp.sqrt(5))/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491687108,"data":"       | p_sym = sp.Integer(1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49168831,"data":"       | q_sym = phi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491689473,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491690585,"data":"       | # define points\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491691765,"data":"       | B = sp.Point(0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491692992,"data":"       | C = sp.Point(p_sym+q_sym, 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491694175,"data":"       | a = p_sym+q_sym\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491695361,"data":"       | I = sp.Point(p_sym, r)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491698283,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491699451,"data":"       | # slopes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491700612,"data":"       | mB = 2*p_sym*r/(p_sym**2 - r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491701823,"data":"       | mC = 2*q_sym*r/(q_sym**2 - r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491703012,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491704177,"data":"       | # A coordinates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491705364,"data":"       | xA = -mC*a/(mB - mC)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491706549,"data":"       | yA = mB*xA\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491707694,"data":"       | A = sp.Point(xA, yA)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491708869,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491709968,"data":"       | # F coordinates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491711137,"data":"       | Fx = p_sym*(p_sym**2 - r**2)/(p_sym**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491712372,"data":"       | Fy = 2*p_sym**2*r/(p_sym**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491713635,"data":"       | F = sp.Point(Fx, Fy)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49171484,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491716214,"data":"       | # line AI\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491717403,"data":"       | line_AI = sp.Line(A, I)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491718584,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491719726,"data":"       | # E as reflection of F across line AI\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491720955,"data":"       | E = F.reflect(line_AI)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491722126,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491723302,"data":"       | # D point\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491724447,"data":"       | D = sp.Point(p_sym, 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491725614,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49172672,"data":"       | # line EF\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491727884,"data":"       | line_EF = sp.Line(E, F)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491729056,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491730162,"data":"       | # N foot from D to EF\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491731386,"data":"       | N = line_EF.projection(D)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491732628,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491733797,"data":"       | # circumcenter O1 of ABC\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491735003,"data":"       | # O1 x-coordinate = a/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491736177,"data":"       | xO1 = a/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491737318,"data":"       | # yO1 expression:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491738515,"data":"       | yO1 = ((xA - xO1)**2 + yA**2 - xO1**2) / (2*yA)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491739786,"data":"       | O1 = sp.Point(xO1, yO1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491740946,"data":"       | R1_sq = (xO1**2 + yO1**2)  # distance to B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491742199,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491743291,"data":"       | # circumcenter O2 of AFE\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491744498,"data":"       | O2 = sp.Point(sp.geometry.Triangle(A, F, E).circumcenter)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491745755,"data":"       | R2_sq = O2.distance(A)**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491748836,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491750004,"data":"       | # vector d = O2 - O1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491751202,"data":"       | dx = O2.x - O1.x\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491752397,"data":"       | dy = O2.y - O1.y\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49175362,"data":"       | d_sq = dx**2 + dy**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491754832,"data":"       | d = sp.sqrt(d_sq)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491756004,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491757114,"data":"       | # a_dist\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491758277,"data":"       | a_dist = (R1_sq - R2_sq + d_sq) / (2*d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491759495,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491760625,"data":"       | # h_sq\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491761858,"data":"       | h_sq = R1_sq - a_dist**2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491763096,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491764223,"data":"       | # unit vector u = (dx/d, dy/d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491765414,"data":"       | ux = dx/d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491766565,"data":"       | uy = dy/d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491767731,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491768886,"data":"       | # point P = O1 + a_dist * u\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49177005,"data":"       | Px = O1.x + a_dist*ux\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49177119,"data":"       | Py = O1.y + a_dist*uy\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491772393,"data":"       | P = sp.Point(Px, Py)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491773573,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491774707,"data":"       | # perpendicular vector to u\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491775871,"data":"       | perp_x = -uy\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491777021,"data":"       | perp_y = ux\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491778229,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491779349,"data":"       | # K = P + sqrt(h_sq) * perp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491780572,"data":"       | K = sp.Point(Px + sp.sqrt(h_sq)*perp_x, Py + sp.sqrt(h_sq)*perp_y)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491781851,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491782971,"data":"       | # Kprime reflection across EF\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491784146,"data":"       | Kprime = K.reflect(line_EF)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491785362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491786454,"data":"       | # determinant for cyclic condition\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491787634,"data":"       | def det_matrix(P1,P2,P3,P4):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491788803,"data":"       |     M = sp.Matrix([[P1.x, P1.y, P1.x**2 + P1.y**2, 1],\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49179003,"data":"       |                    [P2.x, P2.y, P2.x**2 + P2.y**2, 1],\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491791314,"data":"       |                    [P3.x, P3.y, P3.x**2 + P3.y**2, 1],\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49179258,"data":"       |                    [P4.x, P4.y, P4.x**2 + P4.y**2, 1]])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49179382,"data":"       |     return sp.simplify(M.det())\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491804007,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491805159,"data":"       | det_expr = sp.simplify(det_matrix(B, N, K, Kprime))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491808368,"data":"       | det_expr\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491809581,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491811034,"data":"     [Code] [ERROR]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491812273,"data":"       | import sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491813481,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491814635,"data":"       | # define symbols\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491815827,"data":"       | r = sp.symbols('r', positive=True, real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491817095,"data":"       | phi = (1+sp.sqrt(5))/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491818288,"data":"       | p_sym = sp.Integer(1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491819486,"data":"       | q_sym = phi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491820647,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491821788,"data":"       | # define points\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491822979,"data":"       | B = sp.Point(0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491824153,"data":"       | C = sp.Point(p_sym+q_sym, 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491825356,"data":"       | a = p_sym+q_sym\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49182652,"data":"       | I = sp.Point(p_sym, r)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491827685,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491828804,"data":"       | # slopes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491829973,"data":"       | mB = 2*p_sym*r/(p_sym**2 - r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49183123,"data":"       | mC = 2*q_sym*r/(q_sym**2 - r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49183245,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.49183356,"data":"       | # A coordinates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491834726,"data":"       | xA = -mC*a/(mB - mC)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491835897,"data":"       | yA = mB*xA\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491837079,"data":"       | A = sp.Point(xA, yA)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491838246,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491839352,"data":"       | # F coordinates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491840584,"data":"       | Fx = p_sym*(p_sym**2 - r**2)/(p_sym**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491841827,"data":"       | Fy = 2*p_sym**2*r/(p_sym**2 + r**2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491843049,"data":"       | F = sp.Point(Fx, Fy)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.491844224,"data":"       | \n"}
