,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492222001,"data":"       | analysis0.031618875766... This is close to 1/ (something). 1/32 = 0.03125, 1/31.5 = 0.031746. So maybe α = 11 + sqrt(1/32) = 11 + 1/(4*sqrt(2))? sqrt(1/32) = 1/(4*sqrt(2)) ≈ 0.1767767, close but not exact.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.4922236,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492224744,"data":"       | Our value 0.17781697266 is slightly larger.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492225938,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492227111,"data":"       | Maybe α = 11 + sqrt(5)/10? sqrt(5)/10 ≈ 0.2236, too high.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492228416,"data":"       | \n"}
