,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492637936,"data":"       | analysisOur symbolic K gave a different point (negative). This suggests that we selected the wrong intersection (the other side of the chord). The formula K = P + sqrt(h_sq)*perp gives one of the two intersection points; we need to choose the one not equal to A. But we got K far away, maybe the other intersection. Let's compute both possibilities: K1 = P + sqrt(h_sq)*perp, K2 = P - sqrt(h_sq)*perp. Choose the one not equal to A.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492639911,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492641048,"data":"       | Thus we need to compute both and compare.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.4926423,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492643449,"data":"       | Let's modify function to return both.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492644646,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492645829,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef symbolic_K_candidates(p_sym, q_sym, r_sym):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492647109,"data":"       |     B = sp.Point(0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492648288,"data":"       |     C = sp.Point(p_sym+q_sym, 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492649478,"data":"       |     a = p_sym+q_sym\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492650662,"data":"       |     I = sp.Point(p_sym, r_sym)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.492651893,"data":"       |     mB = 2*p_sym*r_sym/(p_sym**2 - r_sym**2)\n"}
