,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2711.495677719,"data":"       | But we already have root that gives ratio ~2.58 (small). There may be another root where ratio large but still satisfies cyclic condition (maybe near where denominator small). That root may be near where D_cross (v_x*k_y - v_y*k_x) is near zero, causing Ox large? Actually Ox = s * w_x where s = (K_norm_sq / 2) / D_cross. If D_cross small, s large, Ox large, ratio may approach limit.\n"}
