,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.169424241,"data":"       | We have set $\\mathcal{F}$ of functions $\\alpha: \\mathbb{Z} \\to \\mathbb{Z}$ with finite support (only finitely many nonzero values). For two such functions $\\alpha, \\beta$, define product $\\alpha \\star \\beta = \\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb{Z}} \\alpha(n) \\cdot \\beta(n)$. So it's like dot product of sequences.\n"}
