,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.169428657,"data":"       | Shift operator $S_n$ defined by $(S_n(\\alpha))(t) = \\alpha(t+n)$. So shift left? Actually $S_n(\\alpha)$ is $\\alpha$ shifted left by $n$? For each $t$, we evaluate $\\alpha(t+n)$. So $S_n(\\alpha)$ is $\\alpha$ shifted by $-n$? Let's not worry.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.169430687,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.16943179,"data":"       | Now a function $\\alpha \\in \\mathcal{F}$ is called \"shifty\" if:\n"}
