,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172210203,"data":"       | We can treat unknowns: $\\beta(t)$ for t in some range, plus unknown k,l (distinct). The equations are infinite but only finitely many nontrivial due to support. Actually the condition $c_n = 0$ for all n not equal to k,l is infinite but many are automatically satisfied because convolution support is limited. For n outside support of convolution, $c_n$ automatically zero; but we also need zeros inside support but not equal to k,l.\n"}
