,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172230554,"data":"       | Let $\\alpha$ be a vector a_0,...,a_8 (integers). Let $\\beta$ be a vector b_t for t in Z (finite support). Let c_n = sum_{i=0}^8 a_i b_{i-n} = 1 if n=k,l else 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172239263,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172240386,"data":"       | Define unknowns b_j for j in Z. Since a_i are zero outside 0..8, only b_{i-n} for i in 0..8 appear. For each n, c_n = sum_{i=0}^8 a_i b_{i-n}.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.17224182,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172242915,"data":"       | Alternatively, fix j = i-n =\u003e n = i-j. So c_{i-j} = sum_{i} a_i b_j. So for each pair (i,j) we have contributions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172244496,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172245592,"data":"       | Thus we can think of convolution as matrix multiplication: define vector b (with indices maybe from some range). Then c = A * b where A is a Toeplitz matrix built from a_i.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172247038,"data":"       | \n"}
