,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.17230761,"data":"       | Thus the condition reduces to: There exists integer d ≥ 1 (since k≠l) such that A(x) divides x^{d} + 1 in the Laurent polynomial ring Z[x, x^{-1}]. Equivalent to: there exists integer polynomial P(x) with integer coefficients such that A(x) = x^m P(x) where P(x) divides x^{d}+1 (in Z[x]) and m is any integer (≥0) such that degree of A ≤8 and all exponents are nonnegative.\n"}
