,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172312205,"data":"       | But since A(x) must have exponents between 0 and 8 inclusive, we can write A(x) = x^{m} P(x) where P(x) is a divisor of x^{d}+1 with constant term nonzero (since P(0) ≠ 0). Then the exponents of A are m + exponents of P. Since exponents of P are between 0 and deg(P). So the max exponent of A is m + deg(P) ≤ 8. Also min exponent is m (since P has constant term nonzero). So m≥0.\n"}
