,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.172842375,"data":"       |         - Then β(x) = x**(-m) * Q(x) = x**(d-m) + x**(-m) ??? Actually (x**d + 1) = P(x) * Q(x). So Q(x) is polynomial. Then β_rev(x) = x**(-m) * Q(x). Wait recall: A(x) * B_rev(x) = x^d + 1. We have A(x) = x^m P(x). So B_rev(x) = x^{-m} Q(x). So B_rev is Laurent polynomial with possibly negative exponents. That's allowed. So define β(t) as coefficient of x^{-t} in B_rev? Actually B_rev(x) = sum b_j x^{-j}. So coefficient of x^{-j} is b_j. So we can extract β values.\n"}
