,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.174768286,"data":"       | Thus the count of shifty α is equal to the number of integer polynomials A(x) with nonnegative exponents up to 8 (i.e., degree ≤8) such that after removing any factor x^r (i.e., ignoring zeros at low degrees), the remaining polynomial divides 1 + x^d for some d≥1.\n"}
