,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.174775261,"data":"       | Thus we need to count all integer divisors of cyclotomic-like polynomials 1 + x^d with degree ≤8, up to multiplication by x^r (where r≥0). But note that multiplication by x^r just adds leading zeros to α (shifts support to the right). Since α must be zero for m\u003c0, we cannot shift left (negative exponent). So we can multiply by x^r for any r≥0 as long as total degree ≤8.\n"}
