,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.174861988,"data":"       | Original condition: There exist integers k≠l such that for all n, (S_n α)⋆β = 1 if n∈{k,l} else 0. This translates to A(x) G(x) = x^k + x^l. Here A(x) = α polynomial (with support 0..8). G(x) = γ polynomial (maybe with negative exponents). We can factor out x^{min exponent of A} = x^r, so A = x^r B where B(0) ≠0. Then we have x^r B * G = x^k (1 + x^d). Let G = x^{k-r} H where H(0) ≠0. Then we get B * H = 1 + x^d.\n"}
