,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.175534347,"data":"       | But we must ensure that we didn't miss any possible B with degree ≤8 that is not product of distinct Φ_{2m}. Could there be other integer polynomials dividing 1 + x^d that are not products of distinct Φ_{2m}? Over Z, any divisor of a product of distinct irreducible polynomials is a product of a subset of those irreducibles (since factorization is unique). So yes.\n"}
