,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.176532944,"data":"       | 8. For a fixed e, any subset of the corresponding cyclotomic factors gives a divisor D, because we can take m whose odd part is the l.c.m. of the odd numbers appearing in the subset.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.176534404,"data":"       | 9. Let L be the maximal allowed degree of D (L = 8−r). For each e we count subsets whose total degree ≤ L. Adding the empty product gives N(L).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.176535897,"data":"       |    Computation yields:\n"}
