,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.176771641,"data":"       | For m=6, need m=6 divides 2d but not d. Since 6=2*3, we need d such that 6|2d =\u003e 3|d. And 6∤d =\u003e either 2∤d or 3∤d? Actually 6∤d means either d not divisible by 2 or not divisible by 3. But we already have 3|d, so need 2∤d. So d must be odd multiple of 3, e.g., d=3. Then x^3+1 = (x+1)(x^2 - x + 1) = Φ_2 * Φ_6. Indeed Φ_6 appears. So m=6 possible.\n"}
