,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.176814997,"data":"       | Thus we need to count number of nonzero integer polynomials A(x) of degree ≤8 that are square-free products of distinct even-order cyclotomic polynomials, up to sign? Actually each distinct product yields two α functions: one with coefficients as given, and its negative. Unless the polynomial is self-negative (i.e., A = -A) which only possible if A=0. So each nonzero product yields two distinct α (unless we consider sign as distinct). So total count = 2 * (number of distinct products). However, there is also possibility that some product yields same coefficient vector as another product? That would be impossible because distinct factorization yields distinct polynomial (since cyclotomic polynomials are irreducible and distinct). So each subset yields distinct polynomial.\n"}
