,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.178483447,"data":"       | Thus we need to find integer polynomial A(x) of degree ≤8 (coeffs a_i) such that there exists integer polynomial C(x) (finite support) with product A(x) C(x) = G(x) where G(x) is a polynomial (or Laurent polynomial?) that has coefficient 1 at two exponents k and l, zero elsewhere. Since k,l can be any integers (positive, negative, zero). So G(x) = x^k + x^l (if we treat coefficient 1). Indeed G(x) = x^k + x^l.\n"}
