,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.178497938,"data":"       | Since we can absorb powers of x into C(x) (i.e., shift exponents), we can set w.l.o.g. k\u003el maybe; then x^l (x^{k-l}+1). So G(x) = x^l (x^{d}+1) where d = k-l \u003e0.\n"}
