,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.178500614,"data":"       | Thus we need A(x) C(x) = x^l (x^{d}+1). Since C(x) can have negative exponents, we can shift the factor x^l into C(x) (or into A(x)). Because A(x) has only nonnegative exponents, we cannot have negative exponent factor in product. So the exponent l must be accounted for by C(x) possibly having exponent l (or negative). Actually product A(x)C(x) has exponents from min exponent of C(x) (call m) to max exponent of C(x)+deg(A). So we can have overall exponent shift.\n"}
