,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.178566452,"data":"       | Thus the condition that A'(x) divides some x^{d}+1 is equivalent to A'(x) being a product of cyclotomic polynomials Φ_m(x) with each m even (i.e., each factor has only roots that are primitive even-order roots of unity). In other words, A'(x) must be a divisor of some x^{d}+1, which is equivalent to A'(x) being a divisor of x^{N}+1 for some N, which is equivalent to A'(x) being a product of cyclotomic polynomials Φ_{2q}(x) for various q.\n"}
