,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.181015582,"data":"       | But we need to be careful: For D=1 (degree 0), shifting by m yields x^m (i.e., δ_m). Multiplying by -1 yields -δ_m (i.e., coefficient -1 at position m). Are both allowed? Let's test: α = -δ_m. Then S_n(α)⋆β = -β(m - n). To get 1 at two positions, we need β such that -β(m - n) = 1 =\u003e β(m - n) = -1 at those n. So choose β = -δ_{m - k} - δ_{m - l}. That's allowed (β can have negative values). So yes, -δ_m works.\n"}
