,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182038646,"data":"       | analysisThus we have 160 distinct α.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.18203982,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.18204094,"data":"       | Now we need to verify that each α indeed satisfies shifty condition by constructing β and k,l.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182042268,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182043414,"data":"       | We'll construct for each α a β as earlier: Choose d = lcm of e's in combo (if combo empty, choose d=1). Then define β' = s * x^{-m} * (1 + x^d) / D. Simplify and verify that β' has integer coefficients (Laurent). Then compute convolution with α to ensure we get 1 at two positions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182045084,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182046133,"data":"       | Let's test for all α.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182047301,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182048388,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef is_shifty(alpha_coeffs):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182049611,"data":"       |     # Convert to polynomial A(x)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182050747,"data":"       |     A = sum(c*x**i for i,c in enumerate(alpha_coeffs))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182051971,"data":"       |     # Determine representation: find D, m, s from alphas2 dict\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182053233,"data":"       |     # Not needed; we can attempt to find k,l,beta by solving linear equations? Use representation we have.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182054535,"data":"       |     return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182055674,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182056728,"data":"       | # Instead, verify using stored representation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182057881,"data":"       | def verify_alpha(combo, deg, m, s):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182058998,"data":"       |     # Build alpha polynomial\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182060166,"data":"       |     D = 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182062909,"data":"       |     for e in combo:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182064088,"data":"       |         D = sp.expand(D * poly_map[e])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182065267,"data":"       |     alpha = sp.expand(s * x**m * D)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182066635,"data":"       |     # Choose d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182067774,"data":"       |     if combo:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182068894,"data":"       |         d = lcm_list(combo)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182070038,"data":"       |     else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182071118,"data":"       |         d = 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182072208,"data":"       |     # Compute beta\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182073367,"data":"       |     beta = sp.expand(s * x**(-m) * sp.simplify((1 + x**d) / D))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182074619,"data":"       |     # Now compute convolution: for n from -10..10 compute inner product with beta\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182075907,"data":"       |     # Since alpha has support 0..8, we can compute S_n(alpha)⋆beta = coefficient of x^{n} in alpha*beta\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182077224,"data":"       |     # Actually product alpha*beta = 1 + x^d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182078366,"data":"       |     prod = sp.expand(alpha * beta)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182079509,"data":"       |     # Should be 1 + x^d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182080608,"data":"       |     if sp.expand(prod - (1 + x**d)) != 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182081761,"data":"       |         return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182082916,"data":"       |     # Now check that there exist k,l distinct such that inner product yields 1 at those n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182084192,"data":"       |     # Since product = 1 + x^d, we have S_n(alpha)⋆beta = coefficient of x^{n} in product? Wait:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182085529,"data":"       |     # (S_n(alpha)⋆beta) = coefficient of x^{n} in alpha * beta? Let's verify:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182086824,"data":"       |     # Convolution (S_n alpha)⋆beta = Σ_t α(t+n) β(t) = coefficient of x^{?}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182088186,"data":"       |     # In polynomial terms, α(x) = Σ α(t) x^t, β(x) = Σ β(t) x^t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182089568,"data":"       |     # Then α(x)·β(x) = Σ_n (Σ_t α(t) β(n - t)) x^n = Σ_n (S_n α ⋆ β) x^n? Actually S_n α ⋆ β = Σ_t α(t+n) β(t) = Σ_t α(t) β(t - n) = coefficient of x^{-n}? Let's derive.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182091419,"data":"       |     # Let product P(x) = α(x)·β(x). Coefficient of x^n in P is Σ_t α(t) β(n - t). That's α ⋆ (shifted β). Not exactly S_n α ⋆ β.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182093009,"data":"       |     # However, we have earlier derived that S_n α ⋆ β = coefficient of x^{?} in α(x)·β(x) after appropriate shift.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182094477,"data":"       |     # Let's compute directly: (S_n α)⋆β = Σ_t α(t+n) β(t) = Σ_u α(u) β(u - n) (set u = t+n). That's coefficient of x^{-n} in α(x)·β(x^{-1})? Not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182095969,"data":"       |     # But we know that α·β = 1 + x^d. So the function f(n) = (S_n α)⋆β is 1 when n = 0? Let's test with example.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182097392,"data":"       |     # Use α = δ_0, β = δ_0 + δ_{-d}. Then α·β = 1 + x^{-d}? Wait.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182100553,"data":"       |     # Let's compute directly using convolution: For α = δ_0 (coeff 1 at 0), β = δ_0 + δ_{-d} (coeff 1 at 0 and -d). Then α·β = 1 + x^{-d}. But we want 1 + x^d. So sign of shift matters.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182102165,"data":"       |     # Actually we derived earlier that α·β' = 1 + x^d ensures that (S_n α)⋆β = 1 at n = k,l for some k,l. Let's verify with example.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182103617,"data":"       |     # Let's test with α = 1 (i.e., α(0)=1). Choose d=3, β' = 1 + x^3. Then α·β' = 1 + x^3. Now compute (S_n α)⋆β' for n values:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182105084,"data":"       |     # α(t) = 1 at t=0 else 0. Then (S_n α)⋆β' = β'(-n) = coefficient of x^{-n} in β'.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182106422,"data":"       |     # Since β' = 1 + x^3, coefficient at -n is 1 if -n = 0 or 3 =\u003e n = 0 or -3. So we get ones at n = 0, -3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182107857,"data":"       |     # So indeed we get two positions (k,l) = (0,-3). So works.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182109044,"data":"       |     # So in general, if α·β' = 1 + x^d, then (S_n α)⋆β' = coefficient of x^{-n} in 1 + x^d = 1 if -n = 0 or d =\u003e n = 0 or -d.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182110509,"data":"       |     # So indeed we get two positions (k,l) = (0, -d). So condition satisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182111735,"data":"       |     # Thus we don't need to check further.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182112931,"data":"       |     return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182114088,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182115163,"data":"       | # verify all alphas2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182116249,"data":"       | all_ok = True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182117383,"data":"       | for combo, deg, m, s in alphas2.values():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182118558,"data":"       |     if not verify_alpha(combo, deg, m, s):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182119733,"data":"       |         all_ok = False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182120838,"data":"       |         break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182121946,"data":"       | all_ok\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182123044,"data":"       | \n"}
