,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.18270605,"data":"       | Since A(x) and D(x) are integer coefficient polynomials (or Laurent). The factorization of x^k + x^l = x^k (1 + x^{l-k}) (assuming k\u003cl). So x^k + x^l = x^k (1 + x^{d}) where d = l - k \u003e 0.\n"}
