,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.182718506,"data":"       | Goal: Count distinct A(x) (i.e., α) such that there exists integer factorization A(x) D(x) = x^k + x^l with k≠l. Equivalent to: there exists integer k,l and integer Laurent polynomial D such that A(x) divides x^k + x^l in the Laurent polynomial ring Z[x, x^{-1}]. Since D must also have integer coefficients.\n"}
