,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.183837675,"data":"       | analysisThe is_shifty_fast still uses sympy division. Let's just test using the condition: is_shifty_fast(t) is heavy; we can skip that and just test if there exists any α not shift of base but still passes divisibility condition. But we can directly test divisibility condition: compute A0 and see if there exists d such that A0 divides 1 + x^d. That's same as checking if A0 is in base_polys (since base_polys is the set of all divisors of 1 + x^d up to degree 8). So we can test for each random α: compute A0; check if A0 in base_polys. If yes, it's shifty; else not. So we don't need to call is_shifty.\n"}
