,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184046894,"data":"       | analysisSympy division still heavy; maybe we can precompute the set of all divisors of 1 + x^d for d up to 30 (which we already have as base_polys). So any divisor of 1 + x^d for d up to 30 is already in base_polys. So there cannot be any new divisor for d up to 30 not in base_polys. However, there could be divisor for d \u003e 30 that is not a divisor for any d ≤30. But earlier we argued that all divisors of 1 + x^d with degree ≤8 appear for d up to 30. Let's verify by enumerating d up to, say, 100 and compare base_polys sets.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184050849,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184051997,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef compute_divisors_up_to(max_d):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184053262,"data":"       |     polys = set()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184054428,"data":"       |     for d in range(1, max_d+1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.1840556,"data":"       |         expr = 1 + x**d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184056786,"data":"       |         coeff, factors = sp.factor_list(expr, modulus=None)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184058015,"data":"       |         factor_polys = [sp.Poly(fac, x, domain='ZZ') for fac, exp in factors]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.18405931,"data":"       |         n = len(factor_polys)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184061199,"data":"       |         for r in range(n+1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184062399,"data":"       |             for subset in itertools.combinations(factor_polys, r):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184063628,"data":"       |                 prod = sp.Poly(1, x, domain='ZZ')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184064842,"data":"       |                 for f in subset:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184065999,"data":"       |                     prod = prod * f\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184067192,"data":"       |                 for sign in [1, -1]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184068397,"data":"       |                     signed = sp.Poly(sign*prod.as_expr(), x, domain='ZZ')\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184069653,"data":"       |                     if signed.degree() \u003c= 8:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2937.184071166,"data":"       |                         polys.add(poly_to_tuple(signed))\n"}
