,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.223948262,"data":"       | But careful: ω is a primitive 13th root, not any root? The product includes all 13 roots, including 1. However ω^0 = 1, so term for k=0 is (2 - 2*1 + 1) = (2 - 2 + 1) = 1. So product includes factor 1 from ζ=1. So product over all roots includes 1 factor. So product = product_{ζ^13=1} f(ζ). That's fine.\n"}
