,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224462237,"data":"       | Thus we need to compute P = ∏_{k=0}^{12} (2 - 2 ω^k + ω^{2k}) = ∏_{z: z^{13}=1} (2 - 2z + z^2). Since the polynomial f(z) = 2 - 2z + z^2 = (z-1)^2 + 1? Let's compute: (z-1)^2 = z^2 -2z +1, so (z-1)^2 +1 = z^2 -2z +2 = 2 - 2z + z^2. Yes. So f(z) = (z-1)^2 + 1.\n"}
