,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224840337,"data":"       | Now e^{i13π/4} = e^{i(12π/4 + π/4)} = e^{i3π + iπ/4} = e^{i3π} e^{iπ/4} = (-1)^3 e^{iπ/4} = - e^{iπ/4} = - (cos π/4 + i sin π/4) = - (√2/2 + i √2/2) = -(√2/2)(1 + i). So a^{13} = 2^{13/2} * (-(√2/2)(1 + i)) = -2^{13/2} * √2/2 * (1 + i) = -2^{13/2} * 2^{1/2} / 2 * (1 + i) = -2^{(13+1)/2} / 2 * (1 + i) = -2^{7} / 2 * (1 + i) = -128/2 * (1 + i) = -64 (1 + i). Yes correct: a^{13} = -64 (1 + i). Good.\n"}
