,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224843524,"data":"       | Similarly, (1 - i)^{13} = conjugate of (1 + i)^{13} because exponent is integer; (1 - i) = sqrt(2) e^{-iπ/4}. Then (1 - i)^{13} = 2^{13/2} e^{-i13π/4} = 2^{13/2} e^{-i3π} e^{-iπ/4} = - e^{-iπ/4} * 2^{13/2} = - (cos π/4 - i sin π/4) 2^{13/2} = - (√2/2 - i √2/2) 2^{13/2} = - (√2/2)(1 - i) 2^{13/2} = -64 (1 - i). Indeed same magnitude but conjugate.\n"}
