,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.22494407,"data":"       | analysisWe need to compute the product over k=0..12 of (2 - 2 ω^k + ω^{2k}) where ω is a primitive 13th root of unity (any non-1 root). Since ω is a 13th root of unity, ω^13 = 1, ω ≠ 1. The product is independent of which primitive root? Probably yes, because the set {ω^k | k=0..12} is the full set of 13th roots of unity (including 1). So product over all 13th roots of unity of that expression.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224945991,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224947171,"data":"       | Let’s define for each root ζ (13th root of unity) the factor f(ζ) = 2 - 2 ζ + ζ^2.\n"}
