,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224952101,"data":"       | We need P = ∏_{ζ^13=1} f(ζ). Since ζ runs over all roots (including 1). The product is a symmetric function of the roots, can be expressed via resultant or evaluation of polynomial.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.22495362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3009.224954733,"data":"       | Observe that f(ζ) = ζ^2 - 2 ζ + 2 = (ζ - 1)^2 + 1. Actually (ζ - 1)^2 = ζ^2 - 2ζ + 1, so plus 1 gives ζ^2 - 2ζ + 2. So f(ζ) = (ζ - 1)^2 + 1.\n"}
