,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3044.528515498,"data":"       | But we need to ensure we didn't double-count subsets where there are more than one pair due to overlapping? Our construction ensures exactly one pair because we exclude adjacent elements to the chosen pair, and we ensure no other pair appears in the remaining intervals (by using f). However, there might be subsets where there is exactly one pair but also includes a longer run of three elements where the middle pair is counted as one pair? Wait, a run of three elements includes two consecutive pairs, so not allowed. So our condition that there is exactly one pair ensures no runs of length \u003e2. So our method should be correct.\n"}
