,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3044.528584855,"data":"       | We can also derive closed form using combinatorial reasoning: number of subsets with exactly one adjacency = sum_{k=1}^{9} F_{k} * F_{10-k}? Wait we used f(L) = F_{L+2}. L = k-2 =\u003e f(k-2) = F_{k}. Since L+2 = (k-2)+2 = k. So f(k-2) = F_{k}. Similarly, R = 8 - k =\u003e f(R) = F_{R+2} = F_{10 - k}. Because (8 - k)+2 = 10 - k. So term for each k is F_{k} * F_{10 - k}. So total = sum_{k=1}^{9} F_{k} * F_{10 - k}. Indeed compute: for k=1..9, sum of product of Fibonacci numbers symmetrical. This sum yields 235.\n"}
