,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3044.528939071,"data":"       | Approach 1: Represent subsets as binary strings of length 10. Exactly one occurrence of \"11\". The block \"11\" can be placed at positions i,i+1 for i=1..9. Then we need to avoid any other \"11\". So we treat the block as a single super-element \"X\" of length 2, and we need to place isolated 1's elsewhere such that they are separated by at least one zero from each other and from the block.\n"}
