,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3044.529168154,"data":"       | We can also give combinatorial reasoning: Choose the unique consecutive pair (i,i+1). Then exclude its neighbors i-1 and i+2 (if exist). The remaining numbers are split into two blocks: left of i-2 and right of i+3. In each block we can choose any subset with no two consecutive numbers. The number of subsets of a block of length n with no two consecutive is F_{n+2}. So sum over i.\n"}
