,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3044.529241695,"data":"       | However, we must be careful about double counting: Could a subset contain two adjacency pairs? No, because we restrict to exactly one adjacency pair; each subset will have exactly one block, and we count it for the i corresponding to that block. But could a subset have a pair that is not unique because there is also a block of size 2 but also another adjacency pair? That would not be counted because we restrict to exactly one adjacency pair. So each subset with exactly one adjacency pair will correspond to exactly one i (the location of the pair). So summation is fine.\n"}
