,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114519707,"data":"       | Given triangle side lengths 13 (AB), 14 (BC), 15 (CA). This is a scalene triangle with sides 13,14,15. It is known to be almost right? Actually 13^2+14^2=169+196=365, 15^2=225; not right. But 13,14,15 triangle is known to have integer area? Let's compute area via Heron: s = (13+14+15)/2 = 42/2 =21. Area = sqrt(s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)) = sqrt(21*8*7*6) = sqrt(21*8*42) = sqrt(21*336) = sqrt(7056) =84. Indeed area 84. So triangle area 84. So altitude from BC? BC=14, area=84 =\u003e altitude from A to BC = 2*area/BC = 168/14 =12. So height from A to BC is 12.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114521844,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114522952,"data":"       | Thus we can place coordinates: Let B = (0,0), C = (14,0) (since BC=14). Then line BC is x-axis. The altitude from A to BC is 12; we need AB=13, AC=15. So A = (x_A, 12) where x_A is such that distances to B and C are 13 and 15.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114526144,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114527301,"data":"       | Compute: AB^2 = (x_A)^2 + 12^2 = 13^2 = 169 =\u003e x_A^2 + 144 = 169 =\u003e x_A^2 = 25 =\u003e x_A = ±5. Since A is above BC, x coordinate can be 5 or -5. Let's compute AC distance: (x_A - 14)^2 + 12^2 = 15^2 =225. Plug x_A=5: (5-14)^2 +144 = (-9)^2+144=81+144=225 correct. So x_A=5 works. x_A = -5 would give distance to C: (-5-14)^2+144 = (-19)^2+144=361+144=505\u003e225, not correct. So A = (5,12). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114529334,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114530481,"data":"       | Thus coordinates: B=(0,0), C=(14,0), A=(5,12). M is midpoint of BC: ((0+14)/2, 0) = (7,0). So M = (7,0).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114531758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114532871,"data":"       | Now line AM passes through A (5,12) and M (7,0). Equation: param t from A to M: A + t*(M-A). Vector M-A = (7-5,0-12) = (2,-12) = (1,-6) scaled. So param: (x,y) = (5,12) + t*(2,-12). When t=0 =\u003e A; t=1 =\u003e M. So line equation.\n"}
