,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114617955,"data":"       | Compute coordinates of P: x = 5 + 2t = 5 + 2*197/148 = 5 + 394/148 = 5 + 197/74 = convert: 5 = 5*74/74 = 370/74, so x = (370+197)/74 = 567/74 = simplify? 567/74 = 7.662... Not simplifiable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114619437,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114620551,"data":"       | y = 12 - 12t = 12 - 12*197/148 = 12 - (2364/148) = 12 - (1182/74) = convert 12 = 12*74/74 = 888/74; subtract 1182/74 =\u003e y = (888-1182)/74 = -294/74 = -147/37 ≈ -3.97297. So P = (567/74, -147/37). Let's check: -147/37 = -3.972972..., yes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114622147,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114623257,"data":"       | Simplify coordinates: x = 567/74, y = -147/37. Note y denominator 37, x denominator 74 = 2*37. So we can express y as -294/74. Indeed -147/37 = -294/74. So P = (567/74, -294/74) = (567, -294)/74 = (567, -294) / 74. So vector coordinates: P = (567/74, -294/74). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114624854,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114625915,"data":"       | Now we have point P.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114627034,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114628111,"data":"       | Now we need point Q on segment AM (i.e., line from A to M) such that angle PBQ = angle PCQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114629395,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114630744,"data":"       | Let Q be a point on line AM between A and M (including possibly interior). Represent Q as param t_q along same line: Q = (5,12) + s*(2,-12) where s between 0 and 1 (since A at s=0, M at s=1). So Q = (5+2s, 12-12s). Then AQ length = s * length AM (since Q is along line from A to M). Actually distance from A to Q = s * |AM|, because the param s corresponds to vector (2,-12) which is the same as AM. Indeed AM length = sqrt(2^2 + (-12)^2) = sqrt(4+144)= sqrt(148) = sqrt(4*37)=2*sqrt(37). So |AM| = 2 sqrt(37). Then AQ = s * |AM| = s * 2 sqrt(37) = 2 s sqrt(37). So we need to find s such that angle PBQ = angle PCQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114632938,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114634041,"data":"       | Define angle PBQ = angle between vectors BP and BQ? Actually angle PBQ is angle with vertex B, formed by lines BP and BQ. So angle between vectors (P - B) and (Q - B). Similarly angle PCQ is angle between vectors (P - C) and (Q - C). Condition: angle between BP and BQ equals angle between CP and CQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114635727,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114636807,"data":"       | Thus we need to find s such that the angle between vectors (P - B) and (Q - B) equals angle between (P - C) and (Q - C).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114638137,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114641047,"data":"       | We can use dot product: For vectors u and v, angle between them satisfies cosθ = (u·v)/(|u||v|). So equality of angles means cosθ1 = cosθ2 (since both angles are between 0 and π). But we need to consider orientation: angles are likely acute? We'll assume positive.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114642821,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114643937,"data":"       | Thus condition: (BP·BQ)/(|BP||BQ|) = (CP·CQ)/(|CP||CQ|). Cross-multiply: (BP·BQ) * |CP||CQ| = (CP·CQ) * |BP||BQ|.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114645361,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114646444,"data":"       | We can square both sides to avoid radicals, but may produce extraneous solutions (like angle supplementary). However since Q is on AM inside segment, likely both angles are acute? Not necessarily but we can check.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114647925,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114649035,"data":"       | Alternatively we can use law of sines in triangles? Might be a known property: Q such that PBQ = PCQ meaning Q is on Apollonius circle? Actually condition that Q sees segment PC under equal angle as B? Wait.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114650537,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114651631,"data":"       | Given point P outside triangle? Actually P is on circumcircle opposite side? Let's examine P coordinates: P is below BC (y negative), while B and C are on x-axis. So P is on circumcircle below BC. So line AP passes through M (midpoint of BC). So P is the antipode of A? Not exactly. Let's compute the reflection of A across BC? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114653341,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114654821,"data":"       | Anyway, Q is on AM (a line from A to midpoint of BC). So Q is interior of triangle? Let's see: A is above BC, M is on BC, so AM is a median from A to BC. Q is somewhere along that median between A and M (including possibly interior). So Q is inside triangle.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114656641,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114657714,"data":"       | Now we need to find s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114658841,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114659938,"data":"       | We can solve equation using algebra.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.11466107,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.11466218,"data":"       | Let’s compute vectors.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114663407,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114664477,"data":"       | Define B = (0,0), C = (14,0). Then:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.11466565,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114666741,"data":"       | BP = P - B = (x_P, y_P) = (567/74, -147/37) = (567/74, -294/74) = (567, -294)/74.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114668011,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114669091,"data":"       | BQ = Q - B = Q = (5+2s, 12-12s).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114670257,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114671365,"data":"       | Similarly CP = P - C = (x_P - 14, y_P - 0) = (567/74 - 14, -147/37) = (567/74 - 1036/74, -294/74) = (-469/74, -294/74) = (-469, -294)/74.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114672741,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114673817,"data":"       | CQ = Q - C = (5+2s -14, 12-12s -0) = (-9+2s, 12-12s).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114675044,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114676141,"data":"       | Now compute dot products.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114679141,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114680374,"data":"       | BP·BQ = (567/74)*(5+2s) + (-294/74)*(12-12s) = (1/74)[567(5+2s) - 294(12-12s)].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114681679,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114682777,"data":"       | Simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114683897,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114685047,"data":"       | Similarly CP·CQ = (-469/74)*(-9+2s) + (-294/74)*(12-12s) = (1/74)[-469*(-9+2s) - 294*(12-12s)]? Wait sign: CP = (-469/74, -294/74). Dot with CQ = (-9+2s, 12-12s). So dot = (-469/74)*(-9+2s) + (-294/74)*(12-12s) = (1/74)[-469*(-9+2s) - 294*(12-12s)]? Actually multiply: (-469/74)*(-9+2s) = (469/74)*(9 - 2s). Because negative times negative yields positive. So that's (469/74)*(9 - 2s). Then plus (-294/74)*(12-12s) = -(294/74)*(12-12s). So sum = (1/74)[469*(9-2s) - 294*(12-12s)].\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114687024,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114688131,"data":"       | Thus both dot products have denominator 74; we can ignore denominator when equating after scaling.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114689444,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114690544,"data":"       | Now compute magnitudes:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114691667,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114692769,"data":"       | |BP| = sqrt( (567/74)^2 + (-294/74)^2 ) = (1/74) sqrt(567^2 + 294^2). Similarly |CP| = (1/74) sqrt( (-469)^2 + (-294)^2 ) = (1/74) sqrt(469^2 + 294^2).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114694161,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114695249,"data":"       | |BQ| = sqrt( (5+2s)^2 + (12-12s)^2 ). |CQ| = sqrt( (-9+2s)^2 + (12-12s)^2 ).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114696485,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114697581,"data":"       | Thus condition:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114698667,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114699747,"data":"       | (BP·BQ) / (|BP||BQ|) = (CP·CQ) / (|CP||CQ|).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114700944,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114702024,"data":"       | Cross-multiply: (BP·BQ) * |CP| * |CQ| = (CP·CQ) * |BP| * |BQ|.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114703318,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114704601,"data":"       | Since BP·BQ and CP·CQ each have factor 1/74, they cancel? Actually each dot product includes 1/74 factor. So both sides have factor 1/74. Also |BP| and |CP| each have factor 1/74. So we can multiply both sides by 74 to simplify.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114706155,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114707275,"data":"       | Let’s compute using sympy rationally and solve for s.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114708527,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114709617,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport sympy as sp\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114710822,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114711914,"data":"       | s=sp.symbols('s', real=True)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114713064,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114714149,"data":"       | # define points\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114715244,"data":"       | B = sp.Point(0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114716354,"data":"       | C = sp.Point(14,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114719294,"data":"       | P = sp.Point(sp.Rational(567,74), sp.Rational(-147,37)) # y = -147/37\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114720552,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114721649,"data":"       | # Q = A + s*(M-A) where s in [0,1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114722841,"data":"       | # A = (5,12), M = (7,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114723994,"data":"       | A = sp.Point(5,12)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114725137,"data":"       | M = sp.Point(7,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114726297,"data":"       | Q = sp.Point(5+2*s, 12-12*s) # as derived\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114727481,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114728549,"data":"       | # vectors\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114729671,"data":"       | BP = sp.Matrix([P.x - B.x, P.y - B.y])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114730817,"data":"       | BQ = sp.Matrix([Q.x - B.x, Q.y - B.y])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114732199,"data":"       | CP = sp.Matrix([P.x - C.x, P.y - C.y])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114733405,"data":"       | CQ = sp.Matrix([Q.x - C.x, Q.y - C.y])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114734577,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114735655,"data":"       | # dot products\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114736797,"data":"       | dot_BP_BQ = BP.dot(BQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114737909,"data":"       | dot_CP_CQ = CP.dot(CQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114739041,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114740094,"data":"       | # magnitudes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114741209,"data":"       | norm_BP = sp.sqrt(BP.dot(BP))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114742387,"data":"       | norm_CP = sp.sqrt(CP.dot(CP))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114743551,"data":"       | norm_BQ = sp.sqrt(BQ.dot(BQ))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114744711,"data":"       | norm_CQ = sp.sqrt(CQ.dot(CQ))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114745879,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114746955,"data":"       | eq = sp.simplify(dot_BP_BQ * norm_CP * norm_CQ - dot_CP_CQ * norm_BP * norm_BQ)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114748219,"data":"       | sp.simplify(eq)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114749321,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.114750381,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
