,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.116778591,"data":"       | 5. Let Q be point on AM: Q = A + t(M-A) with t ∈ [0,1]; coordinates (5+2t, 12-12t). Compute vectors BP, BQ, CP, CQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.1167799,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.116781046,"data":"       | 6. Condition ∠PBQ = ∠PCQ translates to equality of cosines: (BP·BQ)/(|BP||BQ|) = (CP·CQ)/(|CP||CQ|). Square both sides to avoid radicals, leading to equation t(148t-99)(148t-197)^2 = 0.\n"}
