,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117923532,"data":"       | analysisWe need to solve geometry problem. Let's parse.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117924635,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117925739,"data":"       | Triangle ABC with sides AB=13, BC=14, CA=15. So triangle is scalene. M is midpoint of BC. P is point on circumcircle such that M is on line AP (i.e., AP passes through M). So P is second intersection of line through A and M with circumcircle (other than A). So P is the antipode of A with respect to line through M? Actually line AM intersects circumcircle at A and another point P.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117927404,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117928472,"data":"       | We have Q on segment AM such that ∠PBQ = ∠PCQ. So Q is a point on AM such that the angles at B and C subtended by lines BQ and CQ to P are equal. Equivalent: Q is point on AM for which the oriented angles ∠PBQ and ∠PCQ are equal. This condition defines a unique point Q on AM.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117930049,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117931097,"data":"       | Goal: compute AQ length expressed as m/√n, with m,n relatively prime positive integers. Find m+n.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117932334,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117933344,"data":"       | We need to compute AQ.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117934395,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117935434,"data":"       | Let's set up coordinates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117936509,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117937562,"data":"       | We have triangle sides known. Choose convenient coordinate system: Let's place B at (0,0), C at (14,0) (since BC=14). Then we need to locate A such that AB=13, AC=15. So A is somewhere above x-axis (positive y). Coordinates of A: (x_A, y_A) satisfying distance to B: sqrt(x_A^2 + y_A^2) = 13 =\u003e x_A^2 + y_A^2 = 169. Distance to C: sqrt((x_A - 14)^2 + y_A^2) = 15 =\u003e (x_A - 14)^2 + y_A^2 = 225.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117939339,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117940352,"data":"       | Subtract first from second: (x_A - 14)^2 - x_A^2 = 225 - 169 = 56.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.11794148,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117942499,"data":"       | Compute left: (x_A^2 - 28 x_A + 196) - x_A^2 = -28 x_A + 196 = 56 =\u003e -28 x_A = -140 =\u003e x_A = 5.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117943742,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117944785,"data":"       | Then plug into x_A^2 + y_A^2 = 169 =\u003e 25 + y_A^2 = 169 =\u003e y_A^2 = 144 =\u003e y_A = 12 (positive). So A = (5,12). Good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117946103,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117947137,"data":"       | Thus triangle coordinates: B(0,0), C(14,0), A(5,12).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117948244,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117949255,"data":"       | M is midpoint of BC: ((0+14)/2, (0+0)/2) = (7,0).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117950367,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117952694,"data":"       | Now line AM passes through A(5,12) and M(7,0). Equation: param t from A to M: A + t*(M-A) where t from 0 to 1 gives points between A and M. Vector M-A = (2, -12). So param: (x, y) = (5+2t, 12-12t). At t=0 =\u003e A; t=1 =\u003e M.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117954177,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117955206,"data":"       | Now we need P: second intersection of line AM with circumcircle of triangle ABC.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.117956354,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.11795741,"data":"       | First find circumcircle equation. Compute circumcenter O (intersection of perpendicular bisectors). Let's compute using coordinates.\n"}
