,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3102.118045046,"data":"       | Thus P corresponds to t = 197/148 \u003e 1? Let's compute numeric: 197/148 ≈ 1.331. So P is beyond M on line AM extended beyond M (since M corresponds to t=1). Indeed line from A to M continues to P on opposite side of M relative to A? Actually A to M direction vector (2,-12). At t=1 we reach M (7,0). At t\u003e1 we go further beyond M towards (x\u003e7, y\u003c0). So P is beyond BC line maybe below x-axis.\n"}
