,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.353836143,"data":"       | Let Δ = arg(d_a) - arg(d_b) (mod 180°). Then we can add multiples of 30° (mod 180°) because rotating one chord relative to the other by 30° increments (by shifting i vs j) changes Δ by multiples of 30°. So we need to see if there exists integer m such that Δ + 30° m ≡ 90° (mod 180°). This is equivalent to Δ ≡ 90° (mod 30°). Since 30° divides 180°, we can consider modulo 30°.\n"}
