,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.355561172,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.355562377,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure that rectangle sides can also be diameters (step size 6). But we excluded k=6 because chords of step size 6 are diameters, and opposite chords are also diameters but they intersect at center, not parallel. So they cannot serve as opposite sides of rectangle. However could a rectangle have one side as a diameter and opposite side as another diameter offset (parallel)? Two diameters are always intersecting at center (unless they are same line). So they can't be opposite sides. So no rectangles using diameters.\n"}
