,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.355811511,"data":"       | This is a combinatorial geometry problem. Approach: Represent each chord as a line segment connecting two vertices. The set of all chords forms a planar graph (the complete graph drawn on a circle). The rectangles correspond to cycles of length 4 in this planar graph where opposite edges are parallel (i.e., the quadrilateral is a rectangle). However, in the arrangement of chords, many quadrilaterals formed by four intersection points are not rectangles.\n"}
