,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.355939278,"data":"       | Our earlier counting for s even gave 5 chords for each even s (including s=0,2,4,6,8,10). But we might have miscounted for s=6 because the equation 2i ≡ s (mod12) has solutions for s even. For s=6, there are 2 solutions i=3,9 (fixed points). So we have 12-2=10 ordered pairs i≠j, giving 5 unordered chords. Let's list them: For each i from 0 to 11, j = s - i mod12.\n"}
