,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.355971665,"data":"       | Thus there are 7 distinct directions of chords in a regular 12-gon. Let's verify: For a regular n-gon, number of distinct directions of chords (including sides) is floor(n/2)+1? For n even, there are n/2+1 directions: n/2 directions for chords not passing through center (i.e., slopes), plus one direction for diameters (through center). For n=12, n/2+1 = 6+1 = 7. Indeed.\n"}
