,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.356005316,"data":"       | - s=2 (120°) -\u003e +90° = 210° ≡ 30° (since subtract 180). 30° corresponds to direction angle of s? Solve angle = π/2 + π s/12 ≡ π/6 (30°). So π/2 + π s/12 ≡ π/6 (mod π). Subtract π/6: π/2 - π/6 = π/3 = 60°, plus π s/12 ≡ 0 (mod π). So π s/12 ≡ -π/3 (mod π) =\u003e s/12 ≡ -1/3 (mod 1) =\u003e s ≡ -4 (mod 12) =\u003e s ≡ 8 (mod12). So s=8 direction same as s=4 (since s and 12-s same). So s=2 is perpendicular to s=4.\n"}
