oints at (cos30°, sin30°) = (√3/2, 1/2) and (cos150°, sin150°) = (-√3/2, 1/2). So chord is horizontal line y=1/2. Indeed horizontal. Similarly (2,4) connects 60° and 120°, both have y = √3/2? Actually cos60=0.5, sin60=√3/2; cos120=-0.5, sin120=√3/2. So chord is horizontal line y=√3/2. So indeed s=6 chords are all horizontal lines at various y-levels. Good.\n"}
