,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.357831401,"data":"       | Now, condition for perpendicular: orientation of chord (i,j) is angle = π(i+j)/12 + π/2. Two chords are perpendicular if their orientations differ by π/2 (90°). That means (i+j)/12 * π + π/2 differs by π/2 from the other orientation: i.e., (π(i+j)/12 + π/2) - (π(k+l)/12 + π/2) = π/2 (mod π). Simplify: π(i+j - (k+l))/12 = π/2 (mod π). Multiply both sides by 12/π: (i+j - (k+l)) = 6 (mod 12). So chords are perpendicular if i+j ≡ k+l + 6 (mod 12). That is, sums differ by 6 modulo 12.\n"}
