,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358487164,"data":"       | Now verify that all rectangles counted are distinct (no duplicates). Since each rectangle is defined by unordered sets of chords, there may be duplicates if the same rectangle can be formed with different chords? Could a rectangle side lie on more than one chord? As argued earlier, each line determined by two vertices is unique. However, there might be a rectangle side that lies on a chord that is a subsegment of a longer chord that also contains the same line but with different endpoints (i.e., a diameter line passes through two opposite vertices; any chord using those two opposite vertices is the same line; there is only one chord for that line). So no duplicates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35848951,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358490672,"data":"       | But there might be a rectangle where one side lies on a side of the dodecagon (adjacent vertices) and also lies on a diagonal that shares those vertices? For example, side (i,i+1) is a chord. Could there be a diagonal (i, i+7) that also lies on the same line? That would require i, i+1, i+7 collinear. In a regular 12-gon, no three vertices are collinear except opposite pairs (i, i+6). So side (i,i+1) is not collinear with any other vertex besides its endpoints. So the line containing side (i,i+1) passes through only those two vertices. So no other chord shares that line.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35849282,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358493958,"data":"       | Thus each rectangle corresponds uniquely to a set of four chords.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358495183,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358496368,"data":"       | Now we need to confirm that we didn't miss rectangles where the rectangle's sides are not formed by chords but by subsegments of chords that intersect at interior points not at vertices. Our enumeration includes those because we consider chords intersecting inside polygon; the intersection points can be interior. So rectangles with vertices interior are counted.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358498135,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358499289,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure that we counted rectangles where one side is a subsegment of a chord but the opposite side is also a subsegment of a chord that is the same chord but different segment? Not possible because opposite sides must be parallel and distinct lines; they cannot be same chord.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358500924,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358502186,"data":"       | Now verify that each rectangle counted lies entirely within the dodecagon. Since each side is subsegment of a chord connecting two vertices, and chords are inside polygon, the side segment is inside polygon. The rectangle interior is also inside polygon because it's convex combination of points inside polygon. So fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358503904,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358505005,"data":"       | Thus answer 315 seems plausible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358506176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358507311,"data":"       | But we need to double-check that there are no rectangles formed using chords that are not sides of the rectangle but are extended lines beyond rectangle (i.e., rectangle side lies on a chord but not the entire chord). That's fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35851051,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358511646,"data":"       | Now we need to confirm that the problem statement expects integer answer between 0 and 99999. 315 fits.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358512946,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358514072,"data":"       | But we need to verify with known results for similar problems: For a regular n-gon, number of rectangles formed by its sides and diagonals. For n=8 (octagon), there is known answer maybe 36? Let's test our algorithm for n=8 to see if matches known results. This may help verify correctness.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358515715,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358516892,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef count_rectangles_n(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35851815,"data":"       |     # compute chords and families for regular n-gon\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.3585194,"data":"       |     verts = [(math.cos(2*math.pi*k/n), math.sin(2*math.pi*k/n)) for k in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358520695,"data":"       |     # define intersection test using these vertices\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358521934,"data":"       |     def chord_intersection_inside(i,j,k,l):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358523146,"data":"       |         # using orientation test as before\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358524354,"data":"       |         def orient(a,b,c):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358525507,"data":"       |             ax, ay = verts[a]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358526702,"data":"       |             bx, by = verts[b]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35852787,"data":"       |             cx, cy = verts[c]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358529034,"data":"       |             return (bx-ax)*(cy-ay) - (by-ay)*(cx-ax)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358530288,"data":"       |         def sign(x):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358531422,"data":"       |             if abs(x) \u003c 1e-9:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358532662,"data":"       |                 return 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358533808,"data":"       |             return 1 if x\u003e0 else -1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358535062,"data":"       |         o1 = orient(i,j,k)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358536241,"data":"       |         o2 = orient(i,j,l)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358537397,"data":"       |         o3 = orient(k,l,i)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358538542,"data":"       |         o4 = orient(k,l,j)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358539699,"data":"       |         s1,s2,s3,s4 = map(sign,(o1,o2,o3,o4))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358540882,"data":"       |         return (s1*s2 \u003c= 0) and (s3*s4 \u003c= 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358542193,"data":"       |     # generate chords\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358543348,"data":"       |     chords = [(i,j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i+1,n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358544589,"data":"       |     family = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358545766,"data":"       |     for i,j in chords:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358546916,"data":"       |         s = (i+j) % n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358549503,"data":"       |         family.setdefault(s, []).append((i,j))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358550745,"data":"       |     total = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358552103,"data":"       |     for s in range(n//2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358553284,"data":"       |         A = family[s]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358554427,"data":"       |         B = family[(s+n//2)%n]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358555587,"data":"       |         for a1_idx in range(len(A)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358556776,"data":"       |             for a2_idx in range(a1_idx+1, len(A)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358557986,"data":"       |                 a1 = A[a1_idx]; a2 = A[a2_idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358559202,"data":"       |                 for b1_idx in range(len(B)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.35856039,"data":"       |                     for b2_idx in range(b1_idx+1, len(B)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358561609,"data":"       |                         b1 = B[b1_idx]; b2 = B[b2_idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358562804,"data":"       |                         ok = True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358563959,"data":"       |                         for a in (a1,a2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358565151,"data":"       |                             for b in (b1,b2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358566389,"data":"       |                                 if not chord_intersection_inside(a[0],a[1],b[0],b[1]):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358567655,"data":"       |                                     ok=False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358568853,"data":"       |                                     break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358570022,"data":"       |                             if not ok:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358571208,"data":"       |                                 break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358572364,"data":"       |                         if ok:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358573525,"data":"       |                             total += 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358574726,"data":"       |     return total\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358575927,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358577044,"data":"       | for n in [4,6,8,10,12]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.358578204,"data":"       |     print(n, count_rectangles_n(n))\n"}
