,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.359787847,"data":"       | Thus our earlier classification of families as even/odd size is correct.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.359789126,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.359790482,"data":"       | Now for s=0, we have A (size 5) and B (size 5). For pair (2,10) and (4,8) from A, common neighbor count = 5 (i.e., all chords in B intersect both). Indeed (2,10) and (4,8) are \"central\" chords; they intersect all chords from B.\n"}
