,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.359809482,"data":"       | Let's define for a family (sum s). Represent chords as i ranging from 0 to m-1 (i \u003c s-i). The chord (i, s-i) has endpoints i and s-i. Since s is fixed, the chord's position can be described by i (or its distance from the diameter). The diameter corresponds to i = d where s - i = i + m (mod n). The distance between i and d determines the chord's \"level\".\n"}
