,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.359908138,"data":"       | Thus only three pairs have common=5: (1,2), (1,3), (2,3). These are the pairs where at least one chord is the diameter (index 2) and the other chord is adjacent to it (indices 1 or 3) or the pair of chords both adjacent to the diameter? Actually (1,2) includes diameter and chord (2,10) adjacent; (2,3) includes diameter and chord (4,8) adjacent; (1,3) includes two chords (2,10) and (4,8) that are symmetric about the diameter (both on opposite sides). So these are the \"central\" pairs.\n"}
