,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361123054,"data":"       | Let group sizes: For each pair (α,β), size1 = len(dir_groups[α]), size2 = len(dir_groups[β]). Number of ways to choose 2 lines from each group = C(size1,2) * C(size2,2). However not all such rectangles will be inside polygon; some may lie partially outside. So we need to filter.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361124753,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361125854,"data":"       | Let's compute all rectangles and test inside polygon.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361127054,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361128183,"data":"       | We'll generate all combinations: for each pair (α,β), for each unordered pair of lines L1,L2 from group α, for each unordered pair of lines L3,L4 from group β, compute intersection points: P1 = intersection(L1, L3), P2 = intersection(L1, L4), P3 = intersection(L2, L3), P4 = intersection(L2, L4). These four points are rectangle corners.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361131627,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36113296,"data":"       | But we need to ensure they are distinct (lines not parallel within group, they are distinct lines, but they may intersect at same point if lines intersect at a common point, e.g., if L1 and L2 intersect at same point (i.e., they intersect at a vertex). However L1 and L2 are parallel (since same direction), so they cannot intersect unless they are the same line (which we avoid). So they are parallel distinct lines, so they don't intersect. Similarly L3 and L4 are parallel distinct lines.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361134983,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361136097,"data":"       | Thus rectangle is well-defined.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361137284,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361139486,"data":"       | Now we need to test if all four points are inside polygon. Since polygon is convex, rectangle inside polygon if all four vertices are inside polygon.\n"}
