,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361388121,"data":"       | But we need to ensure we counted each rectangle only once. Let's double-check by verifying each rectangle's sides correspond to chords (i.e., each side line appears in chord list). Since we built rectangle from lines L1, L2 (group1) and M1, M2 (group2), those are chords. So each rectangle's sides are chords.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361389807,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361391006,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure we didn't miss any rectangles where sides are chords but rectangle may be degenerate (zero area) or not oriented with perpendicular groups? But rectangle must have right angles. Our construction ensures perpendicular groups (since groups are perpendicular). However there could be rectangles where sides are chords but not from perpendicular direction groups? Actually rectangle must have adjacent sides perpendicular. So the direction groups must be perpendicular. So our enumeration covers all possibilities.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361394581,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361395767,"data":"       | But we need to consider rectangles where sides are chords but the rectangle's sides may be formed by chords of same direction group but not necessarily from perpendicular groups? That's impossible because rectangle sides must be orthogonal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361397321,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361398407,"data":"       | Thus 315 rectangles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361399547,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361401046,"data":"       | But need to verify if there are any rectangles that are counted multiple times due to different pairings of groups? For each rectangle, its sides have two direction groups; there are exactly two groups (horizontal vs vertical). The rectangle may have sides belonging to groups (α,β). Since we only consider each unordered pair (α,β) once (a\u003cb). So each rectangle counted once.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36140296,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361404126,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure we didn't miss rectangles where one side is a chord but the opposite side is also a chord but not from same direction group? Wait opposite sides must be parallel, thus belong to same direction group. So we are good.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361405658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361406778,"data":"       | Now verify that 315 is correct.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361407953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361409093,"data":"       | But we must be careful about rectangles whose vertices lie on the boundary of polygon (i.e., some vertices are polygon vertices). Our point_in_polygon test includes boundary as inside (cross \u003e= -eps). So those rectangles are counted.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36141068,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361411814,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure that rectangle's sides lie on chords within polygon, not partially outside. For a rectangle inside polygon, all four vertices inside polygon ensures the rectangle is inside (since polygon convex). However we must also ensure that each side segment lies on a chord (line) that is within polygon. But if the line extends beyond polygon, the segment inside polygon is the side of rectangle, which is fine. Since chord line is defined by two vertices of polygon; the segment between the two vertices (the chord) lies entirely inside polygon. The rectangle side is a subsegment of that chord, so also inside polygon. So condition satisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361414127,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361415234,"data":"       | Thus 315 seems plausible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361416376,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361417496,"data":"       | But we need to double-check by verifying that each rectangle's sides are subsegments of chords that are fully inside polygon. Since chords are inside polygon, any subsegment is inside. So fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361418937,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36142026,"data":"       | Now verify that there are no rectangles formed by intersection points of chords where sides are not chords (i.e., lines not through any pair of vertices). Could that happen? Suppose we have four intersection points of chords that form a rectangle, but the sides of rectangle are not aligned with any chord line. However if the rectangle's vertices are intersection points of chords, each vertex lies at intersection of two chords. The side connecting two adjacent vertices would be along the line of one of those chords? Not necessarily: The side between vertex A (intersection of chords L1 and M1) and vertex B (intersection of chords L1 and M2) lies along chord L1 (since both vertices lie on L1). So side is part of L1, which is a chord. So rectangle sides always lie on chords. So any rectangle formed by intersection points of chords will satisfy condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361424554,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361425686,"data":"       | Thus enumeration of rectangles formed by intersecting two parallel families of chords (perpendicular) is exhaustive.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361427066,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361428207,"data":"       | Now verify the count by alternative method: maybe we can compute combinatorially.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36142947,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361430594,"data":"       | But before final answer, we should double-check with more robust algorithm: enumerating all unordered quadruples of lines (choose 4 lines from 66) and checking if they form rectangle. That would be C(66,4) ~ 7 million, which is feasible. We'll implement to confirm count.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361432197,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361433337,"data":"       | Implementation: For each combination of 4 lines (i\u003cj\u003ck\u003cl), compute direction groups: we need to check if they can be partitioned into two pairs of parallel lines that are perpendicular. That is: there exist a labeling such that lines a,b are parallel (same direction), lines c,d are parallel (same direction), and direction of a is perpendicular to direction of c. Additionally, the lines must be distinct (no parallel lines overlapping). Then compute rectangle vertices as intersections of a with c, a with d, b with c, b with d, check inside polygon.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361435514,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361436627,"data":"       | But we also need to ensure that the rectangle formed is not degenerate (i.e., lines a and b are distinct parallel lines, not same line). Since each line is unique, that's fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361438051,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361439144,"data":"       | We'll implement brute force to confirm 315.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361440323,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361441434,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport itertools, math\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361442626,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361443707,"data":"       | # Precompute line data\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36144487,"data":"       | line_pairs = [(i,j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i+1,n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361446104,"data":"       | line_data = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361447247,"data":"       | for pair in line_pairs:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361448437,"data":"       |     a,b,c = line_from_pair(pair)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.3614499,"data":"       |     # compute direction angle modulo pi (canonical)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36145113,"data":"       |     dx = verts[pair[1]][0] - verts[pair[0]][0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361452337,"data":"       |     dy = verts[pair[1]][1] - verts[pair[0]][1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361453534,"data":"       |     ang = math.atan2(dy,dx)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361454697,"data":"       |     # canonical as before\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361455887,"data":"       |     if ang \u003c 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36145889,"data":"       |         ang += math.pi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361460103,"data":"       |     if ang \u003e= math.pi - 1e-9:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361461341,"data":"       |         ang = 0.0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361462504,"data":"       |     ang = round(ang,9)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361464347,"data":"       |     line_data.append({'pair':pair,'coeff':(a,b,c),'ang':ang})\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361465588,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361466694,"data":"       | # Map from index to line\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361467836,"data":"       | def is_parallel(i,j):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361469017,"data":"       |     return line_data[i]['ang'] == line_data[j]['ang']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361470287,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361471381,"data":"       | def is_perpendicular(i,j):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36147255,"data":"       |     a1 = line_data[i]['ang']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361473726,"data":"       |     a2 = line_data[j]['ang']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361474856,"data":"       |     # compute diff modulo pi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361476,"data":"       |     diff = (a1 - a2) % math.pi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361477144,"data":"       |     # check if diff ~ pi/2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361478317,"data":"       |     return abs(diff - math.pi/2) \u003c 1e-9 or abs(diff - 3*math.pi/2) \u003c 1e-9\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361479704,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361480773,"data":"       | def rectangle_from_lines(idx1, idx2, idx3, idx4):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361481987,"data":"       |     # assume idx1, idx2 parallel; idx3, idx4 parallel; and idx1 perp idx3\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361483221,"data":"       |     L1 = line_data[idx1]['coeff']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361484396,"data":"       |     L2 = line_data[idx2]['coeff']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36148554,"data":"       |     L3 = line_data[idx3]['coeff']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361486694,"data":"       |     L4 = line_data[idx4]['coeff']\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361487847,"data":"       |     P1 = intersect(L1, L3)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361489024,"data":"       |     P2 = intersect(L1, L4)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361490177,"data":"       |     P3 = intersect(L2, L3)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36149132,"data":"       |     P4 = intersect(L2, L4)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361492457,"data":"       |     if None in (P1,P2,P3,P4):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361493617,"data":"       |         return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361494748,"data":"       |     return (P1,P2,P3,P4)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361495933,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361497018,"data":"       | rect_set=set()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36149821,"data":"       | count=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361499333,"data":"       | # iterate combos of 4 lines\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361500504,"data":"       | total=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361501646,"data":"       | for combo in itertools.combinations(range(len(line_data)),4):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.3615029,"data":"       |     total+=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361505714,"data":"       |     i,j,k,l = combo\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361506907,"data":"       |     # try all partitions into two pairs of parallel lines\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361508207,"data":"       |     # There are 3 ways to partition 4 items into 2 pairs: (i,j)-(k,l), (i,k)-(j,l), (i,l)-(j,k)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361509577,"data":"       |     # For each, check parallel and perpendicular condition\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361510823,"data":"       |     pairs = [((i,j),(k,l)), ((i,k),(j,l)), ((i,l),(j,k))]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361512073,"data":"       |     for (p1,p2) in pairs:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361513637,"data":"       |         a,b = p1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361514806,"data":"       |         c,d = p2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361515938,"data":"       |         if is_parallel(a,b) and is_parallel(c,d) and is_perpendicular(a,c):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361517194,"data":"       |             # ensure lines not coincident (they are distinct)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36151844,"data":"       |             # compute rectangle vertices\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361519667,"data":"       |             rect = rectangle_from_lines(a,b,c,d)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361520884,"data":"       |             if rect is None:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361522038,"data":"       |                 continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361523187,"data":"       |             # check inside polygon\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361524338,"data":"       |             if all(point_in_polygon(p) for p in rect):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361525561,"data":"       |                 # canonical representation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361526796,"data":"       |                 pts = tuple(sorted([ (round(p[0],10), round(p[1],10)) for p in rect ]))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361528086,"data":"       |                 rect_set.add(pts)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361529301,"data":"       |                 break  # break after found one partition\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361530536,"data":"       | # after loops\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361531673,"data":"       | len(rect_set), total\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.361532827,"data":"       | \n"}
