,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363331598,"data":"       | But due to floating errors, we can compute direction vector as a rational pair (dx, dy) where dx = cos(θ_j) - cos(θ_i), dy = sin(θ_j) - sin(θ_i). Since cos and sin of multiples of 30° are rational multiples of sqrt(3)/2 etc. Could use sympy to get exact values. But easier: we can compute direction as complex number difference; we can compute its argument modulo π using sympy's rational approximations maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36333352,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363334822,"data":"       | But we can also compute slope (dy/dx) as rational? Not rational due to sqrt(3). But we can compute direction as a normalized vector (dx, dy) and compare using cross product: two chords are parallel if cross product of direction vectors is zero (or within tolerance). Since direction vectors are exact (maybe using sympy rational + sqrt(3) expressions), we can compute cross product symbolically and test if zero. However, easier: we can compute direction angle using integer pair (Δi) difference in indices? Actually direction vector of chord (i,j) is e^{iθ_j} - e^{iθ_i} = e^{iθ_i}(e^{iΔθ} - 1) where Δθ = 2π (j-i)/n. The direction vector is rotated by angle θ_i plus some base vector depending on step k = j-i (mod n). So direction depends on both i and k. For parallelism, we need direction vectors to be scalar multiples. This occurs when the base vectors (e^{iΔθ} - 1) are parallel after rotating by different θ_i. So we need to find pairs (i,k) and (i',k') such that e^{iθ_i}(e^{iΔθ_k} - 1) is parallel to e^{iθ_{i'}}(e^{iΔθ_{k'}} - 1). This is equivalent to (e^{iΔθ_k} - 1) being a scalar multiple of e^{i(θ_{i'}-θ_i)} (e^{iΔθ_{k'}} - 1). Since scalar multiples can be complex numbers (including rotation). So condition reduces to there exists real λ such that e^{iθ_i}(e^{iΔθ_k} - 1) = λ e^{iθ_{i'}}(e^{iΔθ_{k'}} - 1). Since λ can be negative (parallel opposite direction). Equivalent to direction vectors are parallel if the angle between them is 0 or π.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36333885,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36333993,"data":"       | Thus we can compute direction angle for each chord using arctan2 and group.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363341119,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363342199,"data":"       | Given small n=12, we can just compute numeric angles with high precision and group by rounding to tolerance (like 1e-9). That will be fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363343537,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36334463,"data":"       | Let's implement enumeration and count rectangles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363345776,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363346851,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codeimport math, itertools, collections\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363348033,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363349109,"data":"       | n = 12\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363350238,"data":"       | # vertices coordinates on unit circle\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.3633514,"data":"       | verts = [(math.cos(2*math.pi*i/n), math.sin(2*math.pi*i/n)) for i in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363354325,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363355521,"data":"       | def direction_angle(i,j):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36335666,"data":"       |     # compute angle of vector from i to j\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363357806,"data":"       |     x1,y1 = verts[i]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363358906,"data":"       |     x2,y2 = verts[j]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363360017,"data":"       |     dx = x2 - x1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363361114,"data":"       |     dy = y2 - y1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363362262,"data":"       |     ang = math.atan2(dy,dx)  # range -pi to pi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363363412,"data":"       |     # map to [0, pi) for direction ignoring sign\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36336461,"data":"       |     if ang \u003c 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363366033,"data":"       |         ang += math.pi*2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363367215,"data":"       |     # direction ignoring opposite orientation: map to [0, pi)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363368539,"data":"       |     if ang \u003e= math.pi:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363369676,"data":"       |         ang -= math.pi\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363370946,"data":"       |     return ang\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363372059,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363373233,"data":"       | def chords():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363374375,"data":"       |     ch=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363375617,"data":"       |     for i in range(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363376725,"data":"       |         for j in range(i+1,n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363377991,"data":"       |             ch.append((i,j))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36337909,"data":"       |     return ch\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363380347,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.3633814,"data":"       | def between(a,b,c):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363382662,"data":"       |     # return True if a is strictly between b and c moving clockwise (mod n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363383897,"data":"       |     # assume indices modulo n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363385163,"data":"       |     # We'll treat clockwise as increasing index modulo n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363386366,"data":"       |     # So a is between b and c if (b\u003ca\u003cc) in cyclic order.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363387758,"data":"       |     # Equivalent: (b \u003c a \u003c c) if b \u003c c, else (a \u003e b or a \u003c c) if b \u003e c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363389163,"data":"       |     if b \u003c c:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363390613,"data":"       |         return b \u003c a \u003c c\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363391774,"data":"       |     else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363392892,"data":"       |         return a \u003e b or a \u003c c\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363394168,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363395212,"data":"       | def intersect(ch1,ch2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36339631,"data":"       |     i,j = ch1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363397411,"data":"       |     k,l = ch2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363400777,"data":"       |     # distinct vertices\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36340188,"data":"       |     if len({i,j,k,l}) \u003c 4:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36340305,"data":"       |         return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363404176,"data":"       |     # check interleaving\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363405337,"data":"       |     return (between(i,k,l) != between(j,k,l)) and (between(k,i,j) != between(l,i,j))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363406614,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36340766,"data":"       | # compute direction angles for each chord\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363408829,"data":"       | chords_list = chords()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363409936,"data":"       | angles = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363411006,"data":"       | for ch in chords_list:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363412102,"data":"       |     ang = direction_angle(*ch)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363413216,"data":"       |     angles[ch] = ang\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363414387,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363415457,"data":"       | # group chords by angle (parallel families)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363416582,"data":"       | tol = 1e-9\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363417654,"data":"       | parallel_groups = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363418774,"data":"       | for ch, ang in angles.items():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363419933,"data":"       |     # find key by rounding to nearest tolerance\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363421056,"data":"       |     # we can map to integer by rounding to 1e-6\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363422234,"data":"       |     key = round(ang / (math.pi/1800))  # 0.1 degree resolution? Let's just use tolerance\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363423524,"data":"       |     # Actually better: store list of chords for each angle using approximate equality\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363424742,"data":"       |     # We'll just accumulate manually\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363425888,"data":"       |     found=False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363426977,"data":"       |     for k in parallel_groups:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36342809,"data":"       |         if abs(ang - k) \u003c 1e-9:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363429266,"data":"       |             parallel_groups[k].append(ch)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36343066,"data":"       |             found=True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363431778,"data":"       |             break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363432927,"data":"       |     if not found:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.363434012,"data":"       |         parallel_groups[ang]=[ch]\n"}
