,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364623223,"data":"     [Reasoning] (6598 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36462436,"data":"       | analysisThus not all chords intersect all chords from perpendicular family. Some pairs may be non-intersecting (parallel chords may be \"nested\" such that they don't cross). So we need to count only pairs that intersect.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364625879,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364626982,"data":"       | Thus rectangle count = sum over perpendicular families (A,B) of number of ways to choose two chords from A and two chords from B such that each chord from A intersects each chord from B.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364628437,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364629491,"data":"       | We computed total 60 rectangles.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364630627,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364631668,"data":"       | Now we can attempt to compute analytically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364632831,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364633916,"data":"       | We need to count for each perpendicular pair (A,B) the number of intersecting chord pairs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364635148,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364636303,"data":"       | Let’s denote the chords in a direction family as \"lines\" across the dodecagon. For each direction family, chords are arranged in order (by distance from center). For example, for direction 0° (horizontal), we have chords that are horizontal lines at various heights (y constant). There are 5 chords: three are from step 2, two from step 4? Actually step 2 chords are short diagonals, step 4 chords are longer diagonals, step 6 chords are diameters. For direction 0°, the chords are horizontal: they are diameters (horizontal) and other chords parallel to them (horizontal). These chords are arranged by vertical offset (distance from center). The chords are nested: the diameter passes through the center; other chords are above or below center. For each direction, chords are ordered from topmost to bottommost.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364638958,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364640204,"data":"       | Thus intersection condition: a chord from family A (horizontal) intersects a chord from family B (vertical) if and only if the horizontal chord's y-coordinate range overlaps the vertical chord's x-coordinate range (i.e., they cross). Since chords are straight lines across the interior, any horizontal chord (with y constant) intersects any vertical chord (with x constant) if the x-coordinate of the vertical chord lies within the horizontal chord's x-extent and the y-coordinate of the horizontal chord lies within the vertical chord's y-extent. However, since chords are segments between two vertices, they have finite extents. For a regular polygon, horizontal chords are segments between two points on the circle at same y-level? Actually horizontal chords have endpoints symmetric about vertical axis; they are not necessarily at same y-level; they are horizontal lines (constant y). Their x-extents are from leftmost to rightmost intersection with circle at that y-level. Similarly vertical chords are constant x lines.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364645159,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364646291,"data":"       | Thus a horizontal chord at y = y0 intersects a vertical chord at x = x0 if the point (x0, y0) lies inside the polygon (i.e., within the circle). Since the polygon is convex, any point inside the circle is inside polygon? Actually polygon is inscribed in circle, but polygon is not the whole circle; points near the circle but outside polygon may be outside. However, for regular polygon, the interior is the convex hull of vertices, which is the polygon itself. Points inside the circle but outside the polygon occur near the arcs between vertices. However, for lines at certain y or x, the intersection point may lie inside polygon if both coordinates are within the polygon's interior region. But we can treat intersection condition more directly: Two chords intersect interiorly if their endpoints are interleaved around the circle. For a horizontal chord (i,i+k) and vertical chord (j,j+l), we can test interleaving condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364649005,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364650113,"data":"       | Thus we can count intersecting pairs using combinatorial reasoning based on ordering of vertices.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364651382,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364652424,"data":"       | But perhaps easier: we can compute the number of intersecting pairs between two direction families.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36465369,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364654913,"data":"       | Let’s denote families A (direction α) and B (direction α+π/2). For each chord a in A, define its endpoints as vertices a1 and a2. For each chord b in B, define endpoints b1 and b2. They intersect interiorly iff the endpoints are interleaved: one endpoint of a lies between the endpoints of b (in cyclic order), and the other endpoint of a lies outside that interval. Equivalent to the intervals [a1,a2] and [b1,b2] cross.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364656846,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364657911,"data":"       | Thus for each pair of families, we can count number of intersecting chord pairs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36465914,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364660223,"data":"       | We also need to count rectangles: we need to choose two chords from A that intersect both chords from B. That is, we need to choose a pair of chords from A that intersect both chords from B. Equivalent to: choose two chords from A such that they intersect both chords from B. Since each chord from A intersects each chord from B (if we choose appropriate chords), we need to count number of ways to pick two chords from A and two chords from B such that all four intersections exist.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364662149,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364663276,"data":"       | Thus we need to count the number of 2x2 crossing submatrices in the bipartite intersection graph between chords of families A and B. The bipartite graph has vertices A chords and B chords, edges representing intersecting pairs. We need to count number of complete bipartite subgraphs K_{2,2} (i.e., rectangles). The number of K_{2,2} subgraphs in a bipartite graph can be computed as sum_{pairs of chords a1\u003ca2 in A} (choose number of common neighbors in B choose 2). Or equivalently sum_{pairs of chords b1\u003cb2 in B} (choose number of common neighbors in A choose 2). So we need to compute for each pair of chords in A, how many chords in B intersect both.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364667378,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364668456,"data":"       | Thus we need to compute intersection graph adjacency matrix.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36466967,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364670742,"data":"       | We can compute counts for each pair of families using enumeration to see pattern, then derive formula.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364672014,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364673081,"data":"       | Let's compute intersection adjacency for each perpendicular pair.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364674295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364675372,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef intersection_matrix(dirA, dirB):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364676815,"data":"       |     A = parallel_groups[dirA]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364677955,"data":"       |     B = parallel_groups[dirB]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364679157,"data":"       |     # adjacency: for each a in A, list of b in B intersecting\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364680515,"data":"       |     adj = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364681641,"data":"       |     for a in A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364682757,"data":"       |         adj[a] = [b for b in B if intersect(a,b)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364683937,"data":"       |     return adj\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364685008,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364686111,"data":"       | def count_rectangles_pair(dirA, dirB):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364687262,"data":"       |     A = parallel_groups[dirA]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364688416,"data":"       |     B = parallel_groups[dirB]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364689526,"data":"       |     # compute adjacency\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364690642,"data":"       |     adj = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364691746,"data":"       |     for a in A:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364692844,"data":"       |         adj[a] = [b for b in B if intersect(a,b)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364694039,"data":"       |     # count K_{2,2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364695176,"data":"       |     count = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364696273,"data":"       |     # iterate over unordered pairs of chords in A\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364697428,"data":"       |     for a1,a2 in itertools.combinations(A,2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364698556,"data":"       |         # common neighbors in B\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364699694,"data":"       |         common = set(adj[a1]).intersection(adj[a2])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364700849,"data":"       |         # need at least 2 chords in common\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364701979,"data":"       |         if len(common) \u003e= 2:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.364704917,"data":"       |             count += math.comb(len(common),2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36470615,"data":"       |     return count\n"}
