,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.365252318,"data":"       | Now a rectangle can be formed by choosing two families of parallel lines that are perpendicular to each other. Then choose one line from each family for each pair (i.e., choose two lines from family A (parallel) and two lines from family B (parallel), such that they intersect to form rectangle). However, we need to ensure that the chosen lines intersect inside the dodecagon (the rectangle lies inside). Also need to ensure that the rectangle's sides lie on those lines (i.e., the rectangle's vertices are intersection points of chosen lines). As long as we pick two lines from each family, they intersect to form a parallelogram; if the families are perpendicular, it's a rectangle.\n"}
