,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36526986,"data":"       | Define vertices V_i = (cos(2π i/12), sin(2π i/12)). For each unordered pair (i,j) with i\u003cj, define line L_{i,j} passing through V_i and V_j. Compute its direction vector (dx, dy) = V_j - V_i. Compute normal vector (a,b) = (dy, -dx) (so that a x + b y + c = 0). Compute c = -(a x_i + b y_i). Normalize maybe not needed.\n"}
