,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.365380676,"data":"       | Now we need to count rectangles formed by selecting two directions that are perpendicular. Two directions are perpendicular if the angle between them is 90°, i.e., difference of direction indices corresponds to 3 steps? Let's compute: direction orientation angle = π d / n + π/2 (mod π). So orientation difference between directions d1 and d2 is π (d2 - d1)/n (mod π). For them to be perpendicular, we need difference = π/2 (mod π). That implies (d2 - d1)/n ≡ 1/2 (mod 1). Multiply both sides by n: d2 - d1 ≡ n/2 (mod n). Since n=12, n/2 = 6. So directions that differ by 6 (mod 12) are perpendicular. Indeed, orientation difference of 6 steps (i.e., 180°/12 * 6 = π/2). So direction d and d+6 are perpendicular.\n"}
