,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.366703945,"data":"       | Now we need to count rectangles formed by lines from two families each containing chords of step sizes 1,3,5 (or 2,4,6). The difference in counts may be due to geometry: the lines of odd steps may be more spread out, leading to fewer valid rectangles.\n"}
