,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.366729009,"data":"       | Let's verify that there are no rectangles whose sides lie on the same direction (i.e., rectangle oriented at 45°, not axis-aligned to our chosen families). However, any rectangle's sides are two pairs of parallel lines; each pair must be among the set of lines (chords). Since any line's direction corresponds to some direction index d (0..11). The other pair must be direction d+6 (perpendicular). So any rectangle must be aligned to a perpendicular pair of directions. So we have enumerated all.\n"}
