,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.367915097,"data":"       | But we need to verify if any rectangle counted multiple times within same pair due to swapping of A and B (i.e., rectangle could be counted with a1,a2 swapped or b1,b2 swapped). However, we used combinations for each pair, so order of chords within each family doesn't matter. The rectangle defined by (a1,a2,b1,b2) is counted once per unordered selection of chords from each family. But rectangle may be defined by the same set of four chords but with a1 and a2 swapped (same unordered pair) or b1,b2 swapped (same unordered pair). Since we use combinations, each unordered pair is considered only once. So rectangle counted once.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.367917261,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.367918324,"data":"       | Thus answer 315.\n"}
