,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.367928921,"data":"       | But we need to verify with alternative method or by enumerating all possible rectangles using geometry of intersection points directly. Let's attempt to generate all rectangles as sets of four points (coordinates) that form rectangle and whose sides lie on chords. We'll compute all intersection points of chords (including polygon vertices) and then find all rectangles formed by four such points such that each side lies on a chord (i.e., the segment connecting two vertices lies on a line that is a chord). However, this may be more complex.\n"}
