,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.368353164,"data":"       | analysisThese are chords connecting vertices symmetric about vertex 0? Actually chords (1,11) (adjacent to vertex 0?), (2,10), (3,9), (4,8), (5,7). These are chords that are symmetric with respect to vertex 0 (i.e., reflect across axis through vertex 0 and center). They are all chords that are \"horizontal\" orientation? Actually they are chords that are parallel to each other (vertical/horizontal?). They are all chords that are symmetric about the vertical axis (maybe orientation 0). They are all chords that are \"vertical\" lines? Let's compute orientation for (1,11): i=1, k=10, r = (2*1+10)=12 mod 12 =0. So orientation index 0. The chords are all those that are symmetric about vertex 0 and the opposite vertex 6? Actually (5,7) is across vertex 6? (5,7) passes near vertex 6? Not sure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.368355771,"data":"       | \n"}
