,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.368426601,"data":"       | - If we choose one outer chord (say A1) and one inner chord (A2, A3, A4). Outer chord intersects B2,B3,B4; inner chord intersects all B1..B5. The common intersection set = B2,B3,B4 (since outer chord only intersects those). So again we need to choose 2 out of 3 =\u003e 3 rectangles for each such pair. Number of such pairs: outer chord choices: 2 (A1 or A5). For each outer chord, inner chord choices: 3 (A2,A3,A4). So total pairs = 2*3 =6. Each yields 3 rectangles =\u003e 18.\n"}
