,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.368573165,"data":"       | Case 1: Both B chords are from B_M (i.e., both middle). Then they intersect only A_M. So the A chords must both be from A_M. So choose 2 A chords from A_M (size 2) =\u003e only one possible pair (A3,A4). Choose 2 B chords from B_M (size 2) =\u003e only one pair (B4,B6). This yields 1 rectangle.\n"}
