,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369008108,"data":"       | Thus any pair of chords from the two families intersect (maybe at interior point or at vertex). The rectangle formed by two chords from each family will be a rectangle (maybe degenerate if intersection points coincide? Not possible because chords are distinct and not parallel). So each selection of two chords from each family yields a rectangle.\n"}
