,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369816751,"data":"       | But perhaps there is a simpler combinatorial approach: Count rectangles by selecting four vertices of the dodecagon that form a rectangle? But that only counts rectangles whose vertices are vertices of the polygon, not those with interior vertices. However, many rectangles have vertices at interior intersection points. So we need to count all.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369818459,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369819585,"data":"       | Alternative approach: Use concept of \"grid\" formed by chords of two perpendicular orientations. For each perpendicular orientation pair, we have a set of chords (lines) that intersect each other in a certain pattern. The intersection graph is a bipartite graph with vertices chords of each orientation, edges representing intersections. The number of rectangles is the number of K_{2,2} subgraphs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369821443,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369822585,"data":"       | Thus we can compute the number of rectangles by counting for each pair of chords from orientation d the number of common intersecting chords from orientation d+6, then sum C(common,2). This is what we computed algorithmically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369824083,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36982516,"data":"       | Now we need to find a combinatorial formula for these counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369826325,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369827453,"data":"       | Let's compute for each orientation pair (even/even and odd/odd) the adjacency matrix and compute number of K_{2,2}. Let's compute counts for each pair to see distribution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369828832,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369829887,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codepair_counts = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369832694,"data":"       | for d in range(6):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369833853,"data":"       |     d_perp = (d+6)%12\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369834965,"data":"       |     chords_d = by_orient[d]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369836101,"data":"       |     chords_p = by_orient[d_perp]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369837239,"data":"       |     # compute adjacency sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369838389,"data":"       |     adj = {c: set(p for p in chords_p if chords_intersect(c,p)) for c in chords_d}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369839668,"data":"       |     # count K_{2,2}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369840755,"data":"       |     total = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.36984187,"data":"       |     for c1,c2 in itertools.combinations(chords_d,2):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369843093,"data":"       |         common = adj[c1] \u0026 adj[c2]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369844294,"data":"       |         total += math.comb(len(common),2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369845422,"data":"       |     pair_counts[(d,d_perp)] = total\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.369846562,"data":"       | pair_counts\n"}
