,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.370058799,"data":"       | - Pair of two short chords (both step 2). There are C(2,2)=1 such pair (since there are exactly 2 short chords). Their common intersecting chords? Let's compute: short chords (1,11) and (5,7) intersect which chords of opposite orientation? According to adjacency, each short chord intersects chords (0,6), (1,5), (7,11). Both short chords intersect exactly the same three chords? Let's check: (1,11) intersects (0,6), (1,5), (7,11). (5,7) intersects (0,6), (1,5), (7,11) as well. So common intersecting chords = 3. So this pair yields C(3,2)=3 rectangles.\n"}
