,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":3398.370063864,"data":"       | - Pair of one short and one medium chord (short+medium). There are 2 short * 2 medium = 4 such pairs. Let's compute common intersecting chords for such pair: e.g., short (1,11) and medium (2,10) intersect common chords? Intersection sets: short (1,11): {0,6;1,5;7,11}. Medium (2,10): intersects all 5 chords. Intersection = short's set of 3 chords. So common = 3. Similarly for short with other medium chord (4,8) also 3. So each such pair yields C(3,2)=3 rectangles. So 4*3 = 12.\n"}
